"type\": \"segment\", \"index\": n}` before each segment.","locale":"en"},"8819":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-279","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"Finally `{\"type\": \"end\", \"job_id\": …, \"output_ids\": […], \"output_id\": …}` or `{\"type\": \"error\", \"code\", \"message\", \"detail\"}`.","locale":"en"},"8820":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-280","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"A binary message is always audio; everything else is JSON text. The whole audio is still stored as a result (`output_id`). The client may send `{\"type\": \"cancel\"}` at any time.","locale":"en"},"8821":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-281","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"`granularity` says how fine the audio arrives: `token` as the model emits tokens (CosyVoice, VoxCPM, Qwen3-TTS), `segment` once per segment, `emulated` when the model does not stream and Mizuoto splits the text to emulate it.","locale":"en"},"8822":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-282","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#websocket-apiv1ttsstream","content":"**Streaming text**: with a model that has **Streaming text** (CosyVoice 2 and 3), set `\"text_stream\": true`; `text` is only the beginning. Send the rest as `{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"…\"}` messages and `{\"type\": \"flush\"}` after the last. Leaving before the flush cancels the job.","locale":"en"},"8823":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-283","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-api#http-post-ttsspeakstreamtrue","content":"Where a WebSocket is awkward, add `stream=true` to the same request: the response is the audio as it is made (chunked transfer):","locale":"en"},"8824":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-api-284",