nt":"off","locale":"en"},"9102":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-164","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#check-find-missing-files","content":"Check the archive-type shared files too (a mirror made with `mirror_fetch.py` has them)","locale":"en"},"9103":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-165","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#check-find-missing-files","content":"It sends a HEAD request to each catalogue file's URL, the one Mizuoto itself would download, and prints `complete` or the number of missing files per model; the exit code is 1 when anything is missing.","locale":"en"},"9104":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-166","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#running-your-own-mirror","content":"With several machines on a local network, one machine's models can be laid out as a mirror for the others. The URLs Mizuoto requests from a custom endpoint have this form:","locale":"en"},"9105":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-167","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#running-your-own-mirror","content":"Any Hugging Face compatible server works, and so does a plain static file server whose folders are laid out as `<repo id>/resolve/main/…`:","locale":"en"},"9106":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-168","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#running-your-own-mirror","content":"On a machine with the models downloaded, build the mirror under `<repo id>/resolve/main`:","locale":"en"},"9107":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-169","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#running-your-own-mirror","content":"Or the whole catalogue, downloaded for it: `python scripts/mirror_fetch.py /srv/mirror/team/mizuoto-model/resolve/main`.","locale":"en"},"9108":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-170","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#running-your-own-mirror","content":"Serve `/srv/mirror` with a static file server, for example:","locale":"en"},"9109":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-171","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#running-your-own-mirror","content":"A server that supports HTTP Range lets interrupted downloads resume.","locale":"en"},"9110":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-172","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#running-your-own-mirror","content":"On the other machines:","locale":"en"},"9111":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-173","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#running-your-own-mirror","content":"Downloads then try this server first; files it lacks (and official repository files the custom address does not serve) come from Hugging Face, hf-mirror and ModelScope in turn. `check --endpoint http://192.168.1.10:8000 --repo team/mizuoto-model` tells whether the mirror is complete.","locale":"en"},"9112":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads-174","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-downloads#running-your-own-mirror","content":"See Configuration for every setting, and the FAQ for slow or failing downloads.","locale":"en"},"9113":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"page","content":"Using Mizuoto from Python","breadcrumbs":["Mizuoto Documentation","Advanced"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","locale":"en"},"9114":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-0","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","content":"Call Mizuoto's core services from Python without HTTP, or embed Mizuoto's server and web UI in your own program.","locale":"en"},"9115":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-1","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#calling-the-core","content":"Calling the core","locale":"en"},"9116":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-2","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#opening-the-services","content":"Opening the services","locale":"en"},"9117":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-3","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#the-services","content":"The services","locale":"en"},"9118":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-4","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#speaking","content":"Speaking","locale":"en"},"9119":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-5","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#where-jobs-run","content":"Where jobs run","locale":"en"},"9120":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-6","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#events","content":"Events","locale":"en"},"9121":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-7","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#errors","content":"Errors","locale":"en"},"9122":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-8","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#embedding-the-server","content":"Embedding the server","locale":"en"},"9123":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-9","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#arguments","content":"Arguments","locale":"en"},"9124":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-10","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"Methods and properties","locale":"en"},"9125":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-11"