g`","locale":"en"},"9253":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-139","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"The web UI's address, the port, whether it serves","locale":"en"},"9254":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-140","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"`services`","locale":"en"},"9255":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-141","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"The services the server uses (see above), callable once started","locale":"en"},"9256":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-142","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"The object is also a context manager:","locale":"en"},"9257":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-143","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#methods-and-properties","content":"`serve(block=False, **options)` creates a server with the same arguments, starts it and returns it; with `block=True` it serves in the foreground.","locale":"en"},"9258":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-144","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#pinned-settings","content":"The values in `settings` sit above the settings file and the environment, are **never written to the file**, and cannot be changed through the web UI or the API:","locale":"en"},"9259":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-145","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#pinned-settings","content":"In the web UI's **Settings**, a pinned value is marked **Set by the application Mizuoto runs in** (one set by an environment variable: **Set by an environment variable**). `settings.view().pinned` lists the pinned names.","locale":"en"},"9260":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-146","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#prefix-outside-access-and-the-token","content":"With `api_prefix=\"/voice\"` the web UI is at `<address>/voice/`, the API at `/voice/api/v1/...` and the OpenAI-compatible API at `/voice/v1/...`. The web UI derives the prefix from its own script's URL; nothing else to configure.","locale":"en"},"9261":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-147","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#prefix-outside-access-and-the-token","content":"By default only local names are accepted in `Host` (against DNS rebinding). Behind a tunnel or a reverse proxy, add the public name with `extra_hosts=[\"abc.example.com\"]` or `server.allow_host(\"https://abc.example.com\")`. Requests through such names are never treated as local, so the server-machine-only features (browsing server files and so on) are closed to them.","locale":"en"},"9262":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-148","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#prefix-outside-access-and-the-token","content":"Once it is reachable, anyone with the address can use it: set `access_token`, or add authentication of your own. HTTP API details the access checks.","locale":"en"},"9263":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-149","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#prefix-outside-access-and-the-token","content":"Once started, the server writes `server.json` (`host`, `port`, `url`, `pid`) into the data folder so other programs can find it; `stop()` removes it.","locale":"en"},"9264":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-150","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#mounting-into-an-existing-fastapi-app","content":"When the host program is itself a FastAPI (or other ASGI) application, it can mount Mizuoto instead of opening another port:","locale":"en"},"9265":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed-151","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-embed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-embed#mounting-into-an-existing-fastapi-app","content":"The host enters the child app's `lifespan` on its own event loop (it forwards events to the socket) and calls `services.close()` on the way out. `start_background=True` starts the job scheduler and the unloading of idle models; without it, queued jobs do not run. `create_app` also takes `extra_hosts` (a set; names added to it later are accepted at once) and `serve_ui=False` (the API only).","locale":"en"},"9266":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines","type":"page","content":"Engines in depth","breadcrumbs":["Mizuoto Documentation","Advanced"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-engines","locale":"en"},"9267":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines-0","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-engines","content":"The eight speech synthesis engines and the speech recognition engine one by one: catalogue models, capabilities, voice modes, languages, licences, training methods and what each needs installed.","locale":"en"},"9268":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines-1","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-engines#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance","locale":"en"},"9269":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines-2","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-engines#what-each-engine-needs","content":"What each engine needs","locale":"en"},"9270":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines-3","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-engines#licences","content":"Licences","locale":"en"},"9271":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines-4","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-engines#qwen3-tts","content":"Qwen3-TTS","locale":"en"},"9272":{"id":"/en/