g`, `engine_not_installed`, `asset_missing`","locale":"en"},"11195":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-53","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A model not downloaded; a package the engine needs is not installed (torch, or a licence-gated engine's `mizuoto-fishspeech` / `mizuoto-indextts`); a shared asset missing","locale":"en"},"11196":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-54","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"8","locale":"en"},"11197":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-55","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`device_unavailable`","locale":"en"},"11198":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-56","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A device that does not exist or cannot be used, such as a device naming an unknown remote host","locale":"en"},"11199":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-57","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"9","locale":"en"},"11200":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-58","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`compute_unavailable`","locale":"en"},"11201":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-59","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"No usable device, or not enough free GPU memory (`detail.reason` is `out_of_memory` or `no_device`)","locale":"en"},"11202":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-60","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"10","locale":"en"},"11203":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-61","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`worker_failed`, `engine_error`","locale":"en"},"11204":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-62","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A training stage's process or a remote agent died or stopped answering; the engine raised an exception","locale":"en"},"11205":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-63","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"11","locale":"en"},"11206":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-64","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`timeout`","locale":"en"},"11207":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-65","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"An operation took too long","locale":"en"},"11208":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-66","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"12","locale":"en"},"11209":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-67","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`download_failed`","locale":"en"},"11210":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-68","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A file could not be downloaded from any source","locale":"en"},"11211":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-69","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"14","locale":"en"},"11212":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-70","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`remote_unavailable`","locale":"en"},"11213":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-71","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A remote host cannot be reached, refused the token, or speaks another protocol version","locale":"en"},"11214":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-72","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"130","locale":"en"},"11215":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-73","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`cancelled`","locale":"en"},"11216":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-74","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Ctrl+C, or the job was cancelled","locale":"en"},"11217":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-75","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A missing package looks like this:","locale":"en"},"11218":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-76","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#debugging-and-logs","content":"`MIZUOTO_LOG_LEVEL` sets the log level as well (`DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`; default `INFO`). Each job's full log is `jobs/<job id>.log` in the data folder (`mizuoto job log <job id>`); a training stage's output goes into its job's log too.","locale":"en"},"11219":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-77","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"The command line and a server can open the same data folder at the same time. They are separate processes sharing the settings file, the database and the folders:","locale":"en"},"11220":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-78","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"**Settings**: `mizuoto config set` writes `settings.toml`; a running server reads the change within about a second and the web UI refreshes. The server's address and port take effect the next time it starts.","locale":"en"},"11221":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-79","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"**Jobs**: the command line's jobs are in the database too, so `mizuoto job list` shows the server's jobs and the web UI's **Jobs** panel shows the command line's. Each job records the process that runs it; a process opening the data folder marks unfinished jobs **Interrupted** only when their process has ended, never those of another process still running.","locale":"en"},"11222":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-80","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"**No shared GPU queue**: a command-line job runs at once in its own process, outside the server's GPU queue, and loads its own copy of the model. If the server has the same model loaded on the same GPU, it is in GPU memory twice; when memory runs short, the job fails with `compute_unavailable` (exit code 9).","locale":"en"},"11223":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-81","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"**Loaded models**: `mizuoto runtime` lists the models the running server holds (it finds the server through `server.json` in the data folder) and `mizuoto runtime --unload [MODEL]` unloads them there.","locale":"en"},"11224":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-82","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"**Cancelling**: `mizuoto job cancel` reaches only jobs of its own process and reports `Job … is not running` for a job the server runs. Cancel those with **Cancel** in the web UI's **Jobs** panel, or `POST /api/v1/jobs/{job_id}/cancel`.","locale":"en"},"11225":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-83","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"`mizuoto job retry` runs a failed, cancelled or interrupted job again in the foreground (its stored request is planned again).","locale":"en"},"11226":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-84","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#check-the-engines-download-a-model-speak","content":"Without `-m`, `tts.default_model` is used. `mizuoto model spec <model>` lists the voice modes, languages, common parameters and engine options a model takes.","locale":"en"},"11227":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-85","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#clone-and-design-voices","content":"`-v` takes a voice's id or slug (the first column of `mizuoto voice list`).","locale":"en"},"11228":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-86","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#hear-it-as-it-is-made","content":"`--stream` writes a WAV to stdout as the model makes it, for a player:","locale":"en"},"11229":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-87","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#hear-it-as-it-is-made","content":"`--stream` refuses to write to a terminal; the whole result is still kept, and its path goes to stderr.","locale":"en"},"11230":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-88","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#batches-and-parameters","content":"`-p` sets common parameters (`temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k`, `repetition_penalty`, `max_new_tokens`, `num_steps`, `guidance_scale`, `speed`, `duration`, `seed`, `text_normalization`, `segment_silence_ms`), `-O` the engine's own options; values are parsed as JSON. A parameter the model does not take is dropped with a warning by default, or refused (exit code 4) with `--strict`; the default comes from `tts.strict_params`.","locale":"en"},"11231":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-89","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#training","content":"Every trainer runs in Mizuoto's own environment; each stage runs as a child process of the same Python.","locale":"en"},"11232":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-90","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-completion","content":"Open a new terminal afterwards to complete commands, subcommands and options.","locale":"en"},"11233":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-91","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#next","content":"Command reference: every command's arguments and options.","locale":"en"},"11234":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-92","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#next","content":"Configuration and environment variables: settings, environment variables and the data folder.","locale":"en"},"11235":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-93","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#next","content":"FAQ","locale":"en"},"11236":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"page","content":"Acceleration","breadcrumbs":["Mizuoto Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","locale":"en"},"11237":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","content":"Speed without changing results: the attention dispatcher (sites, references, policies, backends, structured masks, probes), compute.fast, compute.compile, CUDA graphs for decoding steps, sync-free sampling, and the CPU's allocator and thread placement; which opt-in features are not bit-identical.","locale":"en"},"11238":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-1","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"What changes results","locale":"en"},"11239":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-2","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#attention","content":"Attention","locale":"en"},"11240":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-3","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"Sites and their references","locale":"en"},"11241":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-4","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"Policies","locale":"en"},"11242":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-5","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#backends-and-the-chain","content":"Backends and the chain","locale":"en"},"11243":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-6","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#structured-masks","content":"Structured masks","locale":"en"},"11244":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-7","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#probes-and-the-doctor","content":"Probes and the doctor","locale":"en"},"11245":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-8","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#computefast","content":"`compute.fast`","locale":"en"},"11246":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-9","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#torchcompile-computecompile","content":"`torch.compile` (`compute.compile`)","locale":"en"},"11247":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-10","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#cuda-graphs-computecuda_graphs","content":"CUDA graphs (`compute.cuda_graphs`)","locale":"en"},"11248":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-11","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sync-free-sampling","content":"Sync-free sampling","locale":"en"},"11249":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-12","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#cpu-settings","content":"CPU settings","locale":"en"},"11250":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-13","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#for-engine-authors","content":"For engine authors","locale":"en"},"11251":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-14","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","content":"Every engine gives its upstream's output sample for sample on the CPU (see Engines in depth), and speed work keeps it that way: **a default never changes a result**. Faster paths that compute the same kernels with the same arguments (CUDA graphs, fewer waits for the device, CPU memory and thread placement) are on by default. Faster paths that change the arithmetic (other attention kernels, TF32, `torch.compile`, fused projections) are opt-in, and every output lists the ones that ran. Measurements are in Performance record; GPU memory is in Memory.","locale":"en"},"11252":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-15","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"Feature","locale":"en"},"11253":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-16","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"Setting (default)","locale":"en"},"11254":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-17","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"Results","locale":"en"},"11255":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-18","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"CUDA graphs for decoding steps","locale":"en"},"11256":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-19","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"`compute.cuda_graphs` (on)","locale":"en"},"11257":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-20","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"identical to eager","locale":"en"},"11258":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-21","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"Sync-free sampling","locale":"en"},"11259":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-22","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"always","locale":"en"},"11260":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-23","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"identical: the same ids and generator state","locale":"en"},"11261":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-24","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"CPU allocator and thread placement","locale":"en"},"11262":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-25","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"`compute.cpu_allocator`, `compute.cpu_threads` (`auto`)","locale":"en"},"11263":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-26","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"identical","locale":"en"},"11264":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-27","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"Attention as each upstream computed it","locale":"en"},"11265":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-28","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"`compute.attention = auto`","locale":"en"},"11266":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-29","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"identical","locale":"en"},"11267":{"id":"/en/docs/development