on","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#attention","content":"`python -m mizuoto.runtime.accel`: each backend on each device, as JSON","locale":"en"},"11312":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-75","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#attention","content":"`core/compute/accel.py`","locale":"en"},"11313":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-76","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#attention","content":"Installed packages from their metadata and install commands that keep torch (standard library only)","locale":"en"},"11314":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-77","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"A `Site` names one computation and holds its **reference**: exactly what upstream computed there, with the same arguments. Mizuoto declares 19, the dummy engine's included.","locale":"en"},"11315":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-78","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"Reference","locale":"en"},"11316":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-79","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"Sites","locale":"en"},"11317":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-80","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"`sdpa`: SDPA with the call's arguments (the default)","locale":"en"},"11318":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-81","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"most: the Qwen decoder (`qwen`), F5-TTS's DiT, the CosyVoice U-Net and v3 DiT, Seed-VC, HuBERT, BERT, Whisper, GPT-SoVITS's T2S and v4/v5 DiT, Qwen3-TTS's Mimi encoder, VoxCPM's MiniCPM, Fish Speech's prefill and codec, IndexTTS's GPT-2","locale":"en"},"11319":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-82","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"`math_kernel`: SDPA's math kernel called directly","locale":"en"},"11320":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-83","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"Fish Speech's decode steps (`fishspeech.step`)","locale":"en"},"11321":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-84","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"a hand-written softmax","locale":"en"},"11322":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-85","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"Fish Speech's fast transformer (`fishspeech.fast`), IndexTTS's perceiver (`indextts.perceiver`)","locale":"en"},"11323":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-86","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"The attentions that add relative positions inside the scores, or need the probability matrix, are not sites: wenet's relative attention, IndexTTS's Conformer, w2v-BERT, VITS, plus the s3tokenizer (q and k each scaled by d^-¼), MelStyle and G2PW's BERT. They stay hand-written, since no fused kernel computes them. `Site(swappable=False)` keeps a site on its reference whatever the policy; `approx_ok=False` refuses every backend that is not exact.","locale":"en"},"11324":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-87","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"11325":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-88","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"Values","locale":"en"},"11326":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-89","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"11327":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-90","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"`compute.attention`","locale":"en"},"11328":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-91","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"`auto`, `fast`, `sdpa`, `math`, `sdpa_flash`, `sdpa_efficient`, `sdpa_cudnn`, `flash`, `xformers`, `sage`, `sage3`","locale":"en"},"11329":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-92","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"`auto`","locale":"en"},"11330":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-93","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"`engines.<id>.attention`","locale":"en"},"11331":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-94","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"the same, or `inherit`","locale":"en"},"11332":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-95","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"`inherit`","locale":"en"},"11333":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-96","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"`training.attention`","locale":"en"},"11334":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-97","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"the backends with a backward pass (not `sage`, `sage3`)","locale":"en"},"11335":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-98","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"`auto`","locale":"en"},"11336":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-99","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"`compute.attention_strict`","locale":"en"},"11337":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-100","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"a named backend that cannot take a call raises `compute_unavailable` instead of falling back","locale":"en"},"11338":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-101","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"off","locale":"en"},"11339":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-102","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"**`auto` binds nothing**: `attention()` reads one context variable, finds no policy and calls the site's reference (about 1 µs a call).","locale":"en"},"11340":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-103","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"Otherwise the model's `AccelPolicy` is resolved when it loads (`policy_for(name, strict)`: one per value, so models share resolutions) and reported as `LoadedModelInfo.attention`. `LocalHandle` binds it for each step of a request with `RequestContext.accel` (the context variable lives in `runtime/context.py`, so binding loads no torch), so a stream suspended between steps never leaks its policy to another thread.","locale":"en"},"11341":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-104","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"A training stage binds its policy process-wide (`dispatch.PROCESS_POLICY`), because autograd runs backward passes, and gradient checkpointing's recomputed forwards, on threads of its own.","locale":"en"},"11342":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-105","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"A change applies to models loaded afterwards; a change to `engines.<id>.attention` unloads that engine.","locale":"en"},"11343":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-106","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#backends-and-the-chain","content":"Backend","locale":"en"},"11344":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-107","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#backends-and-the-chain","content":"Source","locale":"en"},"11345":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-108","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#backends-and-the-chain","content":"Devices","locale":"en"},"11346":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-109","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#backends-and-the-chain"