ocs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"Case (audio s)","locale":"en"},"12965":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-285","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"graphs off","locale":"en"},"12966":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-286","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"**default**","locale":"en"},"12967":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-287","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"Speed-up","locale":"en"},"12968":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-288","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"clone-en (4.37)","locale":"en"},"12969":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-289","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"7.46","locale":"en"},"12970":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-290","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"**6.23**","locale":"en"},"12971":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-291","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"×1.20","locale":"en"},"12972":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-292","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"clone-zh (3.44)","locale":"en"},"12973":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-293","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"5.90","locale":"en"},"12974":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-294","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"**4.88**","locale":"en"},"12975":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-295","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"×1.21","locale":"en"},"12976":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-296","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"The audio is identical with and without graphs and from run to run, and the real model passes the contract suite on that card (8 passed; 2 skipped: S2 Pro does not stream tokens, and no other engine was installed). The first request after a load takes about 4 s more, with or without graphs (the voice's codes, the first kernels' loading), so capturing the graphs costs little.","locale":"en"},"12977":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-297","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"Where a graphed frame's 64 ms go (`--torch-profile`, clone-en, 95 frames; the device busy 97 % of the time):","locale":"en"},"12978":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-298","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"**Products, about 50 ms**. Each frame reads about 16 GB of weights: the 36 slow layers and the tied output head (about 8 GB), and the 4 fast layers once per codebook (0.8 GB, ten times). The 3060 moves 360 GB/s at most, so the frame cannot take less than about 45 ms. The products run at about 90 % of that.","locale":"en"},"12979":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-299","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"**About 5,900 small kernels a frame, about 14 ms**: norms, rotary embeddings, residual adds, the draws and the eager attention. Each costs the device a few µs whatever its size. Graphs remove the CPU's launches, not that. Only fusing kernels removes it, which changes the rounding (an opt-in, as `compute.compile` is elsewhere). Fish Speech has no compiled path.","locale":"en"},"12980":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-300","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"**The slow layers' eager attention, about 6 ms a frame at 300 positions**, growing with the context. At 600 keys one call takes 330 µs of device time in 22 kernels: the grown cache's `cat`, `repeat_interleave` from 8 to 32 heads, the math kernel's scaled copy of the keys, two products and the mask made additive. Three exact rewrites were checked on the 3060, bit for bit against the current call at lengths 150 to 1,280:","locale":"en"},"12981":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-301","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"passing no mask (the step's is all true);","locale":"en"},"12982":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-302","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"writing the cache in place;","locale":"en"},"12983":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-303","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"keeping the cache expanded to 32 heads.","locale":"en"},"12984":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-304","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fish-speech","content":"The first two save about 5 % of the attention (under 1 % of a frame). The third saves about 20 % (