nce#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"VoxCPM 0.5B LoRA","locale":"en"},"13364":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-684","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"4,967 / 4,343","locale":"en"},"13365":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-685","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"2,616 / 2,747","locale":"en"},"13366":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-686","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"1,216 / 2,747","locale":"en"},"13367":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-687","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"yes (the streamed base too)","locale":"en"},"13368":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-688","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"GPT-SoVITS v2Pro speaker","locale":"en"},"13369":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-689","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"921 / 3,881","locale":"en"},"13370":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-690","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"921 / 3,881","locale":"en"},"13371":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-691","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"921 / 3,881","locale":"en"},"13372":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-692","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"does not repeat on the GPU","locale":"en"},"13373":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-693","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"Fish Speech S2 Pro LoRA","locale":"en"},"13374":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-694","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"14,105 / 9,978","locale":"en"},"13375":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-695","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"14,105 / 9,978","locale":"en"},"13376":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-696","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"14,105 / 9,978","locale":"en"},"13377":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-697","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"its export does not repeat","locale":"en"},"13378":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-698","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"(Since calibrated: memory estimates.) Most estimates are under the peak, some far under (GPT-SoVITS 4×), so the warning before a run says nothing when it should: they need calibrating. `lowest` halves Qwen3-TTS's peak but its host optimizer makes the run 15× slower (152 s before the first step, 6.2 s a step against 0.2 s); most of that was transparent huge pages, now off for such stages (G2, below).","locale":"en"},"13379":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-699","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"Measured on the free GPUs (2026-10-18) against the exact path of the code after G1 (`aeeba79`, frozen), the G0 set with three runs per case.","locale":"en"},"13380":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-700","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"**Done, exact.**","locale":"en"},"13381":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-701","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"**Prefetch only where it pays** (memory): `sequence` handles (autoregressive models; GPT-SoVITS's T2S is one now too) neither prefetch nor reserve room for copies in flight. Partly loaded (G1's caps), interleaved runs on a quiet GPU: Qwen3-TTS base-clone-en 24.6 → 16.2 s, VoxCPM v2-clone-en 29.0 → 13.6 s, CosyVoice v2-clone-en 10.1 → 7.4 s, each equal to no side streams, while F5-TTS and OmniVoice keep their prefetch. The audio is the whole model's.","locale":"en"},"13382":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-702","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"**CosyVoice's flow U-Net under `compute.compile`** recompiled at every request (its per-level attention mask was cached by the mask's identity, which torch.compile guards on): warm requests took 12.8 s instead of 1.0 s. Keyed by the U-Net's level now; compiled, 0.97 s; eager, the same audio as before.","locale":"en"},"13383":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-703","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"**IndexTTS's beam caches in one buffer** (done after the round, measured against `fc4b6b3`, two interleaved rounds): every layer's keys and values sit in one buffer, so a step's beam reorder is one copy per beam (one when no beam moved) and each layer writes its new key and value in place, instead of an `index_select` and a `torch.cat` per tensor, each copying it whole. Two buffers with room to grow take turns. Identical on the GPU and the CPU. Warm: v15-clone-en 0.58 → 0.54 s, v2-clone-en 2.02 → 1.93 s, v25-clone-zh 1.73 → 1.67 s; about 30 s of speech ×1.11–1.12 (1.5 4.79 → 4.29 s, 2 17.57 → 15.81 s); on the CPU ×1.02–1.05.","locale":"en"},"13384":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-704","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"**OmniVoice's packed guidance** (opt-in, request option `packed_guidance`, done after the round against `a552038`): each item's conditional and unconditional sequences in one row under a block-diagonal mask, instead of two rows padded to the conditional length. The exact path is unchanged (identical, the same speed). Packed, two interleaved rounds on a 3090: clone-en 0.77 → 0.61 s, finetuned-en 0.76 → 0.60 s (×1.26–1.27), clone-en-long 3.37 → 3.01 s (×1.12), design-en and auto-zh unchanged (0.54 s: no reference, little padding); the audio is another take (decisions flip under other rounding). On the CPU clone-en 24.0 → 18.3 s (×1.31), design-en ×1.02, both identical to the exact path.","locale":"en"},"13385":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-705","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"**Training under `lowest`** (done after the round, against `a1350b3`, Qwen3-TTS 1.7B's fine-tune on a 3090): its stage spent most of its time in the kernel, compacting memory for each transparent huge page AdamW's per-step temporaries took (sampled stacks: the step's `addcdiv_`), with the page cache filling the RAM. Without huge pages in `lowest` stages (`compute.cpu_allocator` keeps them for the others, whose fine-tunes ran 5–15 % slower without them) and with the host optimizer's copies in one buffer each, moved through a page-locked buffer per dtype: 201 s → 82.8 s (first step 59.5 → 13.3 s, 12.8 → 5.5 s a step), the GPU peak 9.1 → 7.3 GB, weights and losses identical; F5-TTS and OmniVoice under `lowest` unchanged and identical. The rest of a step is CPU AdamW's arithmetic. Profiles of every trainer's standard fine-tune showed no data-loading cost; their host time is checkpoint writing (F5-TTS 4 s of a 9 s stage) and module initialisation draws, which the trainers replay as upstream made them.","locale":"en"},"13386":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-706","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"**`compute.compile`** (opt-in, default inductor mode), warm request and first-request cost against eager:","locale":"en"},"13387":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-707","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"Engine","locale":"en"},"13388":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-708","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"Warm","locale":"en"},"13389":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-709","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"Compile cost","locale":"en"},"13390":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-710","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-optimisation-g2","content":"Audio","locale":"en"},"13391":{"id":"/en/do