 below (with 10 GB of the host swapped) had OmniVoice 12 % slower and two native loads over 100 s: measure such comparisons on a quiet machine. Time to first audio and peak memory: G8 below.","locale":"en"},"13482":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-802","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#against-01-and-the-contract-suite-on-the-gpu-g3","content":"**The contract suite on the GPU** (testing), every installed model, the licence-gated ones included: **144 passed** on the whole `cuda:0` (126 in 52 minutes, and VoxCPM's 18 from its own data folder), and **144 passed** on `cuda:1` capped at 4 GB (`MIZUOTO_TEST_SETTINGS='{\"compute\": {\"vram_limit_mb\": 4096}}'`, less than the large models (Fish Speech S2 Pro, IndexTTS 2, Qwen3-TTS 1.7B) need, so they stream and load partly through the whole stack; 2 h 6 min). The slowest capped test is a long Qwen3-TTS request (the narrator fine-tune's seed test: 2,778 s alone against 322 s whole): an autoregressive model that streams copies its streamed layers once per token.","locale":"en"},"13483":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-803","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#first-audio-and-memory-against-01-g8","content":"2026-10-19, one RTX 3090 (`cuda:0`) on a quiet machine, the G0 cases streamed (`perf/g8/` in the experiment workspace: `run.sh`, `single.sh`, `monitor.py`, which samples the card's used memory and the process tree's RAM every 0.2 s; 0.1's engine workers are counted with its host). Warm request and time to first audio are the best of runs 2–3; `stack.py` records `first_chunk_seconds`.","locale":"en"},"13484":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-804","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#first-audio-and-memory-against-01-g8","content":"Case","locale":"en"},"13485":{"id":"/en/docs/development-pe