g13","content":"1,170","locale":"en"},"13706":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1026","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"2,500 → 1,200","locale":"en"},"13707":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1027","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"F5-TTS","locale":"en"},"13708":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1028","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"1,013","locale":"en"},"13709":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1029","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"799","locale":"en"},"13710":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1030","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"2,500 → 800","locale":"en"},"13711":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1031","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"Qwen3-TTS 1.7B CustomVoice and VoiceDesign take 4,300 (CustomVoice's short case: 4,000), CosyVoice-300M and its instruct variant SFT's 1,900; Drama 3 and F5-TTS's older Base and E2 Base, not measured here, keep their estimates. The 0.6B Qwen3-TTS models, GPT-SoVITS v2Pro, v2ProPlus and v5 Turbo, IndexTTS 2.5 and VoxCPM 0.5B were measured the same way the same day (the CustomVoice model has only a short case).","locale":"en"},"13712":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1032","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"**Gathered transfers, measured and not built.** Copying a streamed unit's weights from one page-locked buffer per unit instead of tensor by tensor (an item of the memory plan) would save each copy's fixed cost. With `vram_mode = none` (nearly every weight streamed) on the same card, Qwen3-TTS's talker copied 222 GB in 32,543 copies (6.8 MB each) at 2.87 GB/s and OmniVoice 26 GB in 6,152 at 2.88 GB/s: the card's link (PCIe x4) carries 2.85 GB/s in one 1 GB copy and 2.82 GB/s in 1 MB ones. On a full x16 link (13.4 GB/s) a 4–7 MB copy takes 0.3–0.5 ms, beside which the few microseconds a copy costs are about 1 %.","locale":"en"},"13713":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1033","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"Measured on the RTX 3090s (2026-10-18), the harness now recording each phase's worst single call (work against its own estimate; a phase's largest work and largest estimate can come from different calls, such as a reference's encoding and a decoding).","locale":"en"},"13714":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1034","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"**Decoders**, bytes per position of output (measured on short and about 30 s texts, then a fifth more): VoxCPM's VAE decoding 1,277 (1.5) and 643 (2) a position against the 256 estimated, its reference encoding 1,395 and 3,100 a sample against 256; Fish Speech's codec 1,922 a sample (the out-of-place Snake since G1 uses more) against 384; IndexTTS's BigVGAN 1,057 (2) and 771 plus 256 MB (1.5) against 256. Since raised, every decoder call, cold or warm, short, long or a batch of 8 (OmniVoice, GPT-SoVITS), stays at or under 82 % of its estimate (IndexTTS 1.5's BigVGAN; Fish's codec 73 %, VoxCPM's VAE 74 %); the closest phase of all is IndexTTS 2's GPT on a long text, 90 %, unchanged and within. Qwen3-TTS 1.7B under an 8 GB cap loads whole; under 4 GB its talker loads partly, and `meta.memory.partial` and the log line say which component, why and with what budget.","locale":"en"},"13715":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1035","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"**Training**, each method with its recipe's default batch (G1 had used the fixtures' smaller ones), peak MB by preset:","locale":"en"},"13716":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1036","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"Fine-tune","locale":"en"},"13717":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1037","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"`standard`","locale":"en"},"13718":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1038","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"`low`","locale":"en"},"13719":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1039","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"`lowest`","locale":"en"},"13720":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1040","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"CosyVoice 2 / 3 `llm` (and 2's `llm_flow`)","locale":"en"},"13721":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1041","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#memory-estimates-calibrated","content":"10,319 / 10,398","locale":"en"},"13722":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1042","page_id":"