nine parts. Most settings are saved as soon as you change them, with **Settings saved**; text fields save when you leave them; **Storage** has its own **Save** button.","locale":"en"},"16303":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"Settings are kept in `settings.toml` in the data folder. Each can also come from an environment variable, such as `MIZUOTO_SERVER__PORT=8000`; a value set that way is marked **Set by an environment variable**, and when Mizuoto runs inside another application it may show **Set by the application Mizuoto runs in**. The settings file and the environment variables are described in full in Configuration and environment variables.","locale":"en"},"16304":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"16305":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"16306":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Language**","locale":"en"},"16307":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"The UI's language; **Auto** follows the browser","locale":"en"},"16308":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Open the browser when the server starts**","locale":"en"},"16309":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Whether `mizuoto webui` opens a browser","locale":"en"},"16310":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Server address**, **Port**","locale":"en"},"16311":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"The address to listen on (`127.0.0.1` by default: this machine only) and the port (7869 by default). **Takes effect the next time the server starts.**","locale":"en"},"16312":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Access token**","locale":"en"},"16313":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Shows **An access token is set** or **No access token**. Type one and click **Set token**; **Clear token** removes it. With a token set, every API request must carry it, and the browser asks for it","locale":"en"},"16314":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Set an access token before letting other machines connect; see Remote access and security.","locale":"en"},"16315":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#compute","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"16316":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#compute","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"16317":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#compute","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"16318":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#compute","content":"**Default 