,"content":"a remove button.","locale":"en"},"16657":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#editing-clips","content":"**Details** holds the name, language and description. At the bottom: **Delete** (to the trash; experiments made from it can no longer run) and **Train on it** (a new experiment on this dataset).","locale":"en"},"16658":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#a-new-experiment","content":"On the **Experiments** tab, click **New experiment** (or **Train on it** on a dataset's page).","locale":"en"},"16659":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#a-new-experiment","content":"**Model to start from**: only installed models that can be trained. Without any, the dialog says which engines can train.","locale":"en"},"16660":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#a-new-experiment","content":"**Training**: the methods for this model; unavailable ones are marked **(not available)** with the reason (shared files missing, the engine not available or on a remote host…). Below are the method's description, its stages, what it makes (**Makes a voice’s own weights** or **Makes a new model**) and the least speech it needs.","locale":"en"},"16661":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#a-new-experiment","content":"**Dataset**; when the dataset has less usable speech than the method needs, creating fails and says how much it has and needs.","locale":"en"},"16662":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#a-new-experiment","content":"**Experiment name**: \"dataset-model\" by default; **Letters, digits, - \\_ and .**","locale":"en"},"16663":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#a-new-experiment","content":"When the result is a voice's weights, **Voice to give the weights**: a library voice, or **A new voice** (made from three of the dataset's clips of 3 to 10 seconds).","locale":"en"},"16664":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#a-new-experiment","content":"The main settings (epochs, learning rate…) can be changed here; **More settings, and the advanced ones, are on the experiment’s page.**","locale":"en"},"16665":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#a-new-experiment","content":"Click **Create**.","locale":"en"},"16666":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#a-new-experiment","content":"An experiment is saved in `experiments/<engine>/<name>/`.","locale":"en"},"16667":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"The experiment's page shows the base model, the dataset, the result and the language. **Stages** is a row of steps, each **Not run**, **Running**, **Done**, **Out of date** or **Failed**.","locale":"en"},"16668":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"Button","locale":"en"},"16669":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"16670":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"**Run**","locale":"en"},"16671":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"Runs from the first stage that is not done (or out of date) to the last; reads **Finished** when all are done","locale":"en"},"16672":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"**Run this stage**","locale":"en"},"16673":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"Runs only the selected stage; the earlier ones must be done","locale":"en"},"16674":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"**Start over**","locale":"en"},"16675":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"After confirming, runs every stage again from the first","locale":"en"},"16676":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"Click a stage to see its description, when it finished and its results, or its error.","locale":"en"},"16677":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"A run is one **Train** job whose steps are the stages; its card shows under the stages.","locale":"en"},"16678":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#stages","content":"**Out of date**: each finished stage records what it read — the dataset, the base model's revision and the settings it uses, and the earlier stages' results. When any of these changes, that stage and every stage after it are **Out of date** (**What this stage read has changed since it ran (the dataset, the model or a setting it uses): run it again.**). Running a stage again also makes the finished stages after it out of date, since they read its old files.","locale":"en"},"16679":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#losses","content":"**Losses** draws the curves live while a training stage runs; switch between training stages when there are several, and turn curves on and off with the chips. Before any data it says **The losses appear here while a training stage runs**.","locale":"en"},"16680":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#settings","content":"**Settings** holds the method's hyperparameters (number fields), the rest under **Advanced**. **Changing a setting makes the stages that use it, and those after them, out of date.** Click **Save** after changing them.","locale":"en"},"16681":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#previews-and-exports","content":"**Previews**: with **Settings › Training › Speak a preview after training** on, the export stage speaks a sample with what was trained; it is listed here.","locale":"en"},"16682":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#previews-and-exports","content":"**Exported**: the exported **Voice** (**Open** it or **Use in Speak**) or **Model** (**Models** opens the Models screen). Exported weights are added to the chosen voice; an exported model appears in the model list as `engine/name`.","locale":"en"},"16683":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#previews-and-exports","content":"**Delete** at the bottom moves the experiment and its work files to the trash; what it exported stays.","locale":"en"},"16684":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#cpu-and-gpu","content":"A fine-tune needs a GPU in practice. The smallest card each one runs on, with its recipe's default batch, by **Memory** setting (the peaks measured on an RTX 3090, with the estimate's margin: a tenth more and 512 MB):","locale":"en"},"16685":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#cpu-and-gpu","content":"Fine-tune","locale":"en"},"16686":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#cpu-and-gpu","content":"Standard","locale":"en"},"16687":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#cpu-and-gpu","content":"Low","locale":"en"},"16688":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#cpu-and-gpu","content":"Lowest","locale":"en"},"16689":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#cpu-and-gpu","content":"CosyVoice 2 / 3, `llm` (2's `llm_flow` alike)","locale":"en"},"16690":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#cpu-and-gpu","content":"12 GB","locale":"en"},"16691":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#cpu-and-gpu","content":"12 GB","locale":"en"},"16692":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#cpu-and-gpu","content":"12 GB","locale":"en"},"16693":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#cpu-and-gpu","content":"F5-TTS `full`","locale":"en"},"16694":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"