ontent":"Uninstalling","locale":"en"},"16936":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-9","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Mizuoto is one Python distribution: the server, the web UI, the command line and every engine run in one Python environment. Install **torch** first, in the build for your hardware, then **Mizuoto**. The two licence-gated engines (Fish Speech, IndexTTS) are distributions of their own, installed beside Mizuoto when you want them.","locale":"en"},"16937":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-10","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"16938":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-11","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"Requirement","locale":"en"},"16939":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-12","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"Operating system","locale":"en"},"16940":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-13","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"Linux, Windows, macOS","locale":"en"},"16941":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-14","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"Python","locale":"en"},"16942":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-15","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"3.10–3.14","locale":"en"},"16943":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-16","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"torch","locale":"en"},"16944":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-17","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"2.8 or newer (2.9 or newer on Python 3.14, the first with its wheels), the build for your hardware (CUDA, ROCm, XPU, Apple silicon or CPU)","locale":"en"},"16945":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-18","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"Disk","locale":"en"},"16946":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-19","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"A few GB for torch, plus the models","locale":"en"},"16947":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-20","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"GPU","locale":"en"},"16948":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-21","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"An NVIDIA GPU is recommended; AMD (ROCm, Linux), Intel (XPU) and Apple silicon (MPS) work too (not yet tested on real hardware), and every engine also runs on a CPU, slowly","locale":"en"},"16949":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-22","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"Network","locale":"en"},"16950":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-23","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"Installing reaches PyPI and the PyTorch download site; downloading models reaches Hugging Face, hf-mirror or ModelScope (chosen in **Settings › Downloads**)","locale":"en"},"16951":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-24","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"No system programs are needed: audio decoding, resampling and the text front ends ship in Python wheels.","locale":"en"},"16952":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-25","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"Mizuoto is on PyPI as `mizuoto`; the licence-gated engines are `mizuoto-fishspeech` and `mizuoto-indextts`. Use a virtual environment of your choice. Install torch first, from the index that matches your machine, so that installing Mizuoto keeps that build:","locale":"en"},"16953":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-26","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"Then Mizuoto, in one install; add the gated engines when you want them:","locale":"en"},"16954":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-27","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"uv works the same way: `uv pip install mizuoto` in a virtual environment.","locale":"en"},"16955":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-28","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"You need uv, and bun to build the web UI.","locale":"en"},"16956":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-29","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"The full development setup is in Development setup.","locale":"en"},"16957":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-30","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"One image holds the server, the UI and every engine, with GPT-SoVITS's Japanese and Korean front ends; models go to the `/data` volume.","locale":"en"},"16958":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-31","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"Build argument","locale":"en"},"16959":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-32","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"16960":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-33","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"16961":{"id":"/e