dropping speech"],[16158,"A blank line"],[9993,"A CA bundle, or the agent's own certificate when it is self-signed"],[11118,"A CA bundle, or the agent's own certificate when it is self-signed; empty: the system's CAs"],[9944,"A cache of the files hosts sent: `<cache>/remote/files/<sha256>/`"],[9194,"A call with `wait=True` runs the job on the calling thread and returns it finished. Ctrl+C while it runs cancels it (the job comes back with `state == \"cancelled\"`). A job submitted without `wait` **does not run**: there is no scheduler"],[16804,"A cast of voices reads a book, a script or a dialogue line by line"],[16855,"A cast of voices reads a book, a script or a dialogue line by line, each speaker with its own model and voice; changed lines are rendered again, and a chapter or the whole project is exported as one file with subtitles."],[11342,"A change applies to models loaded afterwards; a change to `engines.<id>.attention` unloads that engine."],[14418,"A change to an engine's code takes effect in a new process: restart the server, or run the command again."],[14335,"A change to any `engines.<id>.*` setting unloads that engine's models (`unload_engine`), so the next request loads them with the new device, dtype or load options."],[16428,"A clip"],[16476,"A clip longer than the model allows follows **Settings › Speech › A reference clip too long for a model**: by default **Cut it to fit** (at the quietest point before the limit; its transcript is then dropped), or **Refuse it**."],[10160,"A clip whose emotion to borrow"],[12049,"A command"],[9688,"A command runs its job in the foreground in its own process: it does not queue with the server's GPU jobs and loads its own models, so the same model can be loaded in GPU memory twice."],[12289,"A command-line process has no models loaded; the server does"],[10164,"A common parameter `name=value` (repeatable)"],[12655,"a component used outside its phase fails (it was not placed);"],[14314,"A CPU kernel trap found while checking E2-TTS against upstream: `F.linear` on a strided (non-contiguous) 3-D input takes another kernel when the weight requires grad, or when it is an *inference tensor* (made inside `torch.inference_mode()`), even under `no_grad`. Upstream's weights are ordinary parameters that require grad, so native engines leave parameters as `nn.Module` makes them (no `requires_grad_(False)`), and models are loaded outside inference mode. Requests still run inside it. The engine reference has both traps."],[11420,"a CUDA graph is capturing and the backend is not `graph_safe`. Captures include attention (VoxCPM's local diffusion step, Fish Speech's fast transformer, Qwen3-TTS's code predictor); `graph_safe` is set only where a capture was replayed over new inputs and equalled the eager call on them (RTX 3060, torch 2.8): `sdpa`, `math`, `sdpa_flash`, `sdpa_efficient`, `sdpa_cudnn`, `flash` 2.8.3 and `xformers` 0.0.32. SageAttention 1.0.6 captured too, but the same backend runs 2.x, unchecked, and `sage3` was not tried. A backend that raises inside a capture is not marked broken: the capture fails, the step runs eagerly, and the backend is tried there."],[11878,"A database whose schema is newer than the running version is logged (an older Mizuoto shows relative records of a newer one as missing; nothing is deleted)."],[16603,"A dataset is saved in `datasets/<name>/` in the data folder: `dataset.json`, `manifest.jsonl` with one row per clip, and FLAC clips in `audio/`."],[16463,"A description in words (Qwen3-TTS VoiceDesign, VoxCPM2), or choices from fixed attributes (OmniVoice)"],[14420,"A development machine's GPUs may be full with another process's work. Put the engine on the CPU then: `mizuoto config set engines.qwen3tts.device cpu`, or `MIZUOTO_TEST_DEVICE=cpu` for the contract suite. A model always tries to load; when the GPU's memory runs out, the job fails with `compute_unavailable` (exit 9) and every model not in use is unloaded from the GPUs."],[8682,"A device is missing or unusable"],[11198,"A device that does not exist or cannot be used, such as a device naming an unknown remote host"],[8702,"A download failed from every source"],[14139,"a dummy-engine `mizuoto speak`;"],[11484,"A failed capture can also leave its error pending in the CUDA runtime after the capture has ended (torch 2.15, CUDA 13.2), and the check after the thread's next kernel launch reports it once (allocating, copying, reading back and synchronizing do not, nor did a `zero_()`): `take_pending_error` runs a little eager work (an allocation, a copy from the host, a kernel, a read back) until it runs, dropping that report, so the eager fallback starts clean (`scripts/graph_failure_probe.py` shows which cleanup a torch release needs)."],[11483,"A failed capture swaps in a fresh generator in the same state (an aborted capture leaves the old one unusable), and the caller runs eagerly; it is logged once."],[16235,"A failed line does not stop the others: it is marked **Failed** with the reason, and the rest go on."],[11172,"A failing command prints the error and, when the error names a fix, the command to run on the next line; the exit code tells the kind of error. The codes are defined in `mizuoto/core/codes.py`, each error class's exit code in `mizuoto/core/errors.py`:"],[9199,"A failure **while the job runs** raises nothing: `speak(..., wait=True)` returns a job with `state == \"failed\"` and the cause in `job.error` (`code`, `message`, `detail`). What raises is what can be found before running (an unknown model, invalid parameters, a licence not accepted…). The error codes are listed in HTTP API."],[11167,"A few details:"],[16946,"A few GB for torch, plus the models"],[14464,"A few rules across engines are held here too:"],[12056,"A field with a default and a docstring in its group in `core/settings/models.py`; when the UI shows it, a control in Settings, the text in both languages and `typegen`; document it in both language versions of Configuration. A change to