was not finished, or a shared file it needs is missing"],[8990,"A folder without `model.json` (the download did not finish), or a shared file it needs is missing"],[9693,"A forgotten token is replaced by setting a new one on the server machine."],[15361,"A frame is one slow-transformer step and ten codebooks. The plain loop waited for the device about 22 times a frame: the end-of-turn check; a masked assignment zeroing the codebook embeddings of non-semantic tokens (`vq_sum[~mask] = 0` reads the mask back); the fast transformer's mask and rotary rows taken with list indices (two copies to the device per codebook); a Python boolean stored into a device tensor in the sampler, twice per draw. Each became an exact equivalent (`torch.where`, slices, `fill_`), and the decoding step's mask is made as the one all-true row it is. One wait per frame remains."],[15735,"A frame is one talker step and fifteen code-predictor steps: some 6 000 small kernels, launched one by one by the CPU. The plain loop also waited for the device about 35 times a frame (`torch.multinomial`'s two validity checks per draw, the suppressed ids copied to the device at each step, the padding check, the EOS check), and each wait drained the GPU's queue. `decode.py` removes this without changing a result:"],[15396,"A frame is ten codes: the backbone predicts its main token (the end of the turn or a semantic token, whose place in the band is code 0) from the frames so far, each prompt row's embedding being its token's plus, for audio rows, its code 1 (scaled by 1/√2). The tower then takes the backbone's hidden state and draws codes 1–9, one residual layer per code, its first shared layer also seeing the previous frame's codes 2–9. Text is cut into chunks of about 300 UTF-8 bytes with at most three speakers each (sentence ends, then clause marks, then spaces; never inside a tag or bracket), each generated with the first chunk and the latest one in its prompt as history; `single_chunk` generates the whole text at once."],[14517,"A fresh `torch.Generator` seeded with *s* against the default stream after `torch.manual_seed(s)`"],[14544,"A full request through Mizuoto's stack: native against reference, same seed, same torch"],[14126,"A gated package names the Mizuoto versions it works with in its `pyproject.toml`: `mizuoto>=0.2.0,<0.3`. Its code runs on Mizuoto's runtime and its manifest (options, catalogue, licence) ships in `mizuoto`, so:"],[12395,"A generator: `yield AudioChunk(samples, sample_rate, segment, final)` as soon as each piece is ready, calling `ctx.check_cancel()` at every step; record the values actually used in `ctx.applied` and warnings with `ctx.warn()`"],[8934,"A GPU machine can serve as a remote host from the same image, running `mizuoto agent` instead of the web UI:"],[16597,"a GPU with 24 GB recommended"],[11321,"a hand-written softmax"],[12562,"A handle's **minimum** is its fixed parts plus the copies of its largest units the streamer holds at once."],[12559,"A handle's `kind` decides which units stay resident when not all fit, after the `hot` ones:"],[11838,"A handle's methods are `prepare_voice`, `synthesize` / `convert` / `edit` (generators: the engine runs only inside `next()`, each step with the request context bound and `torch.inference_mode()` entered) and `call(op, payload)` (ASR's `transcribe`, Fish Speech's `codec_*`, `mizuoto.snapshot`). Loading runs outside inference mode. The details are in Runtime."],[8921,"A health check every 30 s on `http://127.0.0.1:7869/api/v1/app/health` (which needs no token)."],[16649,"a histogram of **Clip lengths**;"],[11871,"A host and its remote agents must speak the same protocol version and refuse each other otherwise."],[11861,"A host application can pin values with `settings_overrides`."],[9093,"A Hugging Face compatible address"],[8962,"A Hugging Face mirror, often faster in mainland China"],[10749,"A Hugging Face token, sent to huggingface.co only (never to a mirror) when downloading models"],[17067,"A job card appears at the bottom of the page; when it is done the result is listed under **Results**. Click its play button."],[12059,"A job kind"],[11872,"A job records its process; opening the data folder marks only jobs whose process is gone `interrupted`, so a second command does not interrupt a render in progress."],[14889,"A job worker's stdout (events) and stderr (libraries) reach the host on one pipe, so an event can arrive glued to a progress bar's unfinished `\\r` line. The host splits lines at the event prefix (`parse_lines` in `mizuoto/core/jobs/jsonl.py`); before that, every metric after a progress-bar redraw was lost."],[9730,"A job's log"],[11422,"A kernel that raises (anything but running out of memory or a cancel) is marked broken for that call, and the next backend takes it. Running out of memory propagates to the exact retry. Each fallback is logged once per (site, backend, reason). The request's `Run` counts what it used, and the output records it with a warning when anything fell back:"],[15451,"a larger v2Pro SoVITS"],[10142,"A library voice (id or slug)"],[8844,"A library voice (id or slug); or a preset speaker of the model; or one of OpenAI's names (`alloy`, `ash`, `ballad`, `cedar`, `coral`, `echo`, `fable`, `marin`, `nova`, `onyx`, `sage`, `shimmer`, `verse`), which fall back to the model's own voice, or its first preset speaker when it has no voice of its own. Any other name is 404"],[8771,"A library voice's id or slug"],[11192,"A licence-gated engine (Fish Speech, IndexTTS) whose licence is not accepted yet"],[16447,"A licence-gated engine (Fish Speech, IndexTTS): opens the licence dialog"],[16002,"A licence-gated engine: its distribution, such as `pip install mizuoto-indextts`."],[16098,"A line about the engine. When it is not available, what it needs: **Needs** *torch* (or *mizuoto-indextts*…)**, which is not installed: mizuoto doctor says how to install it.** Every engine is part of Mizuoto except the licence-gated ones, which are packages of their own (see First run)."],[16155,"A line of that speaker (see the rules below)"],[16157,"A line of the narrator"],[11901,"A loaded engine serves one request at a time; a training run holds it too"],[14905,"A log line"],[16189,"a menu:"],[11217,"A missing package looks like this:"],[12284,"A missing transcript is looked up in the cache while planning, else transcribed in the job; without ASR, `clone_no_transcript` or an error with a hint"],[11852,"A missing transcript is transcribed first when `tts.auto_transcribe` is on and ASR is ready (cached by audio SHA-256, model and beam width in the `transcripts` table, and saved into the voice); otherwise the model's `clone_no_transcript` is used, or the request fails with `capability_not_supported` and the install command."],[14357,"A Mizuoto development setup has two parts: one Python environment (`.venv`) with torch, Mizuoto installed editable and the development tools, and bun for the web UI and this site. Every engine runs in that one environment; there is nothing else to build. Everyday tasks run through `scripts/dev.py`, which uses only the standard library, behaves the same on Linux, macOS and Windows, and runs the same tools CI runs."],[8842,"A Mizuoto model id; or an alias from `tts.model_aliases`; otherwise `tts.default_model`; with none of them, 404"],[8678,"A model is not downloaded, a package the engine needs is not installed (torch, `mizuoto-fishspeech`, `mizuoto-indextts`; `detail.missing` lists them), a shared file is missing"],[9773,"A model loads on first use, in the server's process, on its engine's device, and stays loaded for the next request:"],[11195,"A model not downloaded; a package the engine needs is not installed (torch, or a licence-gated engine's `mizuoto-fishspeech` / `mizuoto-indextts`); a shared asset missing"],[12475,"A model runs whenever its smallest working set fits the device, not only when all of it fits. Mizuoto's runtime does this the way ComfyUI does (`load_models_gpu`, `ModelPatcher`'s partial loading, dynamic VRAM), without a native allocator: a request places only the components its current step needs; when they do not fit, other components give up memory unit by unit; when that is still not enough, the components load partly and the rest of their weights stream from RAM as each layer runs. Running out of memory becomes slower, not failed."],[9703,"A model that does not fit its GPU loads partly: the layers that fit stay on the GPU and the rest of its weights stream from RAM as they run (slower; the result says so). Mizuoto always tries to load a model, whatever the estimate says, and fails with `compute_unavailable` (exit code 9, HTTP 503; `detail.reason` is `out_of_memory`) only when an allocation really fails. It then unloads every model not in use from every GPU, as ComfyUI does. You can:"],[16441,"A model that is not ready can still be chosen. The **Speak** button at the bottom is then replaced by the **first** thing it needs; click it to start, with its progress:"],[14485,"A model that streams tokens sends its first audio within three quarters of a three-sentence request (GPT-SoVITS v2 with fixed-length chunks: it cuts at pauses by default)"],[14483,"A model that streams: the sink hears its variant's granularity, gets more than one piece of one segment when it streams tokens, and the stored output is the pieces joined"],[16323,"A model unused this long is unloaded"],[10234,"A model with speech editing, e.g. `f5tts/v1-base` (required)"],[10217,"A model with voice conversion, e.g. `cosyvoice/cosyvoice2-0.5b` (required)"],[8654,"A model, voice, job, output or engine is unknown"],[16751,"A model's preset speaker, for that model only"],[10382,"A model's preset speakers"],[8981,"A model's state:"],[12543,"A module may name its units with `memory_units() -> list[nn.Module]`. Otherwise each child of a `ModuleList` or `Sequential` of at least 1 MB is a unit (the outermost lists; a unit is never split further)."],[16480,"A moment after you stop typing, the box shows how Mizuoto will cut long text (**N segments**, one chip each), or **The engine splits long text itself** when the model handles long text. The parameter **Pause between segments (ms)** sets the silence between segments."],[12298,"A name cannot be both a command and a group: `mizuoto env vars`; parameter presets are `--use-preset/-P`, since `--preset` is the preset speaker"],[8658,"A name clash, or a clash with an operation in progress"],[11186,"A name exists already; a stage is running; `webui` finds no free port"],[11337,"a named backend that cannot take a call raises `compute_unavailable` instead of falling back"],[14763,"A new branch, a manual run, a list the compare API cuts short (300 files) or a failure to read it checks everything; `tests/test_ci.py` covers the mapping."],[16153,"A new chapter, titled with the text after `#`"],[15080,"A new CLI command is also added to `EXPECTED_TREE` in `tests/cli/test_cli.py`."],[16549,"A new dataset"],[16555,"A new experiment"],[16576,"a new model"],[16584,"a new model"],[16592,"a new model"],[16580,"a new model (a CustomVoice model whose preset speaker is the voice)"],[16588,"a new model (a LoRA keeps the base weights beside its adapters)"],[16596,"a new model (still under the Fish Audio research licence)"],[16124,"A new project"],[16148,"A new project starts with one speaker, **Narrator**."],[12031,"A new third-party dependency goes into `pyproject.toml` and into its layer's allowed list in `tests/test_architecture.py`, with the reason it is needed (see Release)."],[16732,"A new voice"],[14794,"A newer run of the same branch cancels the older one. A push to `main` that changes a version file starts the release workflow, which runs `ci.yml` as its checks for what the push changed; CI's own run of that push skips every job (`scope` sees the version file), so the checks run once. Tags start only the release workflow, whose checks are everything. Pushing the docs site to GitHub Pages is `site.yml`'s, not CI's (see Release)."],[10281,"A note about the voice"],[10182,"A parameter preset (`mizuoto preset list`); `--param` and `--option` win over it"],[12277,"A partial mirror works: what it lacks comes from the official repositories file by file, checked against the same SHA-256"],[15822,"A patch is the DiT's Euler steps (each a guidance pair), the local encoder, the stop head and both language models' steps: some 6 000 small kernels, and three waits for the device (the stop flag and each language model's position copied from a Python integer). `model.PatchDecoder` runs a patch over fixed tensors with one wait, for the stop flag. The language models step before the flag is read (upstream reads it first and stops before stepping); they draw nothing and their caches are dropped when generation ends, so the patches are the same. A full cache raises where upstream's step would."],[12275,"A path on one machine means nothing on another"],[10464,"A payload value `key=value` (repeatable)"],[10785,"A PEM certificate (chain): serve HTTPS. Browsers on other machines let a page record the microphone only over HTTPS"],[12498,"A phase of a request; `run` adds the exact retry and the fallback"],[14297,"A phase of the request: its components placed with room for its working memory; `run` adds the exact retry after running out of memory and the optional fallback (Memory)"],[12594,"A phase under `ctx.use` (one that yields audio or consumes a generator) is not retried, so its estimate must bound what it can reach."],[12644,"A phase's estimate decides whether its weights fit whole, so it is sized by the request (its text tokens, batch rows, the reference's length), not by the worst case `max_new_tokens` allows. Setting aside memory the request never uses pushes weights out for nothing: a worst case of 8192 frames, doubled, was 2.4 GB for a Qwen3-TTS sentence that uses about 20 MB."],[12050,"A plain function in `mizuoto/cli/commands/` with `--json`, registered in `get_app()` of `cli/app.py` (name and help at registration), and added to `EXPECTED_TREE` in `tests/cli/test_cli.py`. See Adding a command"],[16653,"a play button and its length;"],[16187,"a play button for the line's take in use;"],[10695,"A port in use makes it try the next ones (up to 20); when all fail it exits with code 3, and with code 4 when a certificate file does not exist. Binding to an address other than loopback logs a warning that other machines can reach the server. Once started, it prints `SERVER_READY url=http://...` on standard output."],[10148,"A preset speaker of the model"],[10483,"A project is a book, script or dialogue read line by line by a cast of voices. A script is plain text: `#` starts a chapter, `Name: text` is a line of that speaker, a blank line ends a paragraph."],[16141,"A project is saved in `projects/<name>/project.json` in the data folder."],[12272,"A project's lines render as ordinary speak jobs; takes are outputs of kind `line`, stale by request fingerprint"],[16180,"A project's page has three tabs: **Script**, **Cast** and **Export**. The top shows its name, the save state (**Saving…**, **Saved**, **Unsaved changes**) and rendered lines out of all, with their length."],[11904,"A project's render (which submits ordinary speak jobs)"],[15419,"A random model with the real one's shapes but 8 experts did run, on an RTX 3060 (2026-11-03, torch 2.8, bf16, 8.5 GB on the device). Every token still uses 8 experts, so a decoding step does the real model's work."],[12647,"A rare generation that outruns its estimate under `ctx.run` runs again with more weights streamed, exactly."],[14356,"A real engine on your machine"],[10273,"A reference clip (repeatable, required)"],[10999,"A reference clip outside the model's length window: `trim` cuts it at its quietest point before the limit (its transcript no longer matches and is dropped), `reject` refuses it"],[10144,"A reference clip to clone (repeatable)"],[11572,"A refused WebSocket is closed with 1008. socket.io's `connect` handler (`SocketBridge._on_connect`) checks `auth.token` once more."],[14038,"A release produces three distributions: `mizuoto` (wheel and sdist, with the built web UI inside, every engine under a permissive licence included) and the wheels of the two licence-gated engines, `mizuoto-fishspeech` and `mizuoto-indextts`. All three install into one environment over a torch the user chose, and each is versioned, checked and released on its own. This page covers how they are built, checked and published to PyPI (with twine, by the release workflow)."],[12570,"A reload from page-locked copies only queues them: placing S2 Pro's 9 GB returns in 0.9 s, and the copies take 2 s more on an RTX 3060. The request's next wait for the device then waited for all of them without checking for a cancel, so a cancel made right after an unload waited 2.6 s. A phase whose handles gained resident weights on a CUDA device now waits for those copies itself (`manager._await_copies`, an event polled every 5 ms) and checks for a cancel meanwhile. It does so only inside a request, and other phases keep running without a wait. The cancel then takes 0.4 s, and the model stays loaded, its copies finishing on their stream."],[12274,"A remote agent owns its models and engines; requests carry files by content (SHA-256); training stays local"],[8706,"A remote host cannot be reached, refused the token or speaks another protocol"],[11213,"A remote host cannot be reached, refused the token, or speaks another protocol version"],[17041,"A remote host needs the same Mizuoto version as this machine: update both."],[11139,"A remote request whose agent stays silent this long fails (seconds, 10–3600)"],[16774,"a remove button (one clip must remain)."],[16656,"a remove button."],[9903,"A request is batched only when all of these hold:"],[12051,"A route"],[12125,"A route's dependencies are in its signature and tests can pass isolated services; no graph nodes need to share services"],[16677,"A run is one **Train** job whose steps are the stages; its card shows under the stages."],[14877,"A run is one `train` job whose steps are the selected stages:"],[10735,"A running server reads changes to the file within about a second, and open web UIs refresh; saving in the web UI afterwards merges with the file as it is, so it keeps the command line's changes. A broken file makes the server log `Ignored a change to … settings.toml` and keep its settings. `server.host`, `server.port` and the certificates take effect the next time the server starts; changing `engines.<id>.*` unloads that engine's models, which load with the new settings when next used."],[10713,"A sample `settings.toml`"],[14295,"A scratch folder under `<cache>/scratch/<engine>/`, removed when the call ends"],[12063,"A screen"],[14489,"A seeded request gives the same audio before and after another engine's model ran in the process"],[9109,"A server that supports HTTP Range lets interrupted downloads resume."],[12055,"A setting"],[9985,"A short name, used in engine devices (`gpu-box/cuda:0`); not empty, without `/` or `.`"],[12128,"A single user or a small trusted group running it locally; the complexity pays only for multi-tenant serving"],[12415,"A source clip and a voice; a clip, its transcript and `EditSpan`s"],[15424,"A source review against upstream found Mizuoto cutting Drama 3's long text itself (fixed: the variant declares `long_text`) and float16's experts unclamped (fixed), and the request-level differences listed under Deviations."],[8975,"A source that answers 401, 403 or 404 for a file, or serves it with the wrong size or SHA-256, is left for the next one at once. Other errors (a dropped connection, a timeout, a 5xx) are retried on the same source up to 4 times, after 1, 2, 4 and 8 seconds (30 at most). When every source fails, the job ends with `download_failed` (exit code 12); its detail lists the sources tried and the last errors. The job log has one line per file naming the source it came from."],[9295,"a speaker"],[16883,"a speaker"],[16228,"A speaker's settings stay when its model (or the project's) changes, so choosing the first model again brings them back. Each line's request carries only the style instruction, parameters and engine options its model takes; the rest are kept but not used. A kept instruction the model does not follow (or not with this voice) says so under the field, and **Add a style instruction** is not offered for that speaker's lines. A preset speaker or a language the new model lacks is marked on the card: those decide what is said, so the lines fail until you choose again."],[12096,"A Stable Diffusion model manager"],[14891,"A stage method returns a JSON-serialisable dict, stored as the stage's `result`; later stages read it from `ctx.results`. `StageContext` (`mizuoto/training/context.py`) offers:"],[12269,"A stage that logs is evidently alive; a silent one still beats"],[16184,"a state dot (hover for the state's name; see the next section);"],[12123,"A static service locator, `ApiDependencies.invoker`"],[15516,"A streamed middle chunk too short for the SOLA overlap leaves an empty piece, on which upstream's post-processing raises an error; kept as upstream behaves. It has been seen with a `min_chunk_length` of 4."],[12563,"A streamed unit's weights rest in RAM. Forward pre- and post-hooks on the unit, and on each module holding its weights, swap `param.data` to a device copy for the call and back after it. Hooks on the leaves make any path into a layer work (`layer.forward_step(…)`, `vae.decode`), and nothing in `ops` or in a layer's code changes. A component wholly on its device has no hooks at all, so the resident path costs nothing."],[8758,"A synthesis can wait for its result: `POST /api/v1/tts/speak?wait=true&timeout=600` answers with the finished job; `result.output_id` (and `result.output_ids` for a batch) is the result's id. When the job is still running after `timeout` seconds (600 by default, at most 3600) the answer is 504 `timeout` with the job in `detail.job_id`; it goes on, and you read it as usual."],[10283,"A tag (repeatable)"],[9376,"A text in a language whose optional extra is missing fails with `capability_not_supported` and the install command in the hint, for instance `pip install 'mizuoto[gptsovits-ja]'`."],[14885,"A thread emits a `HeartbeatEvent` every 10 s (`HEARTBEAT_SECONDS`)."],[8698,"A time limit passed (for example `wait=true`)"],[14890,"A trainer is a `mizuoto.training.Trainer` subclass with one `stage_<id>(ctx)` method per stage id its methods declare; `ctx.request[\"method\"]` says which method runs. The trainer's module imports no torch at the top: the host imports it to read `REQUIRES` and `DEVICES` (`InferenceService.trainer_needs`) and to ask `refuses(method, model_dir)`, which says, without torch, why a method cannot start from a model (Qwen3-TTS: the 0.6B Base for `speaker`; the method then shows as unavailable, and a run cannot start), so the maths lives in modules it imports inside the stage methods. CosyVoice's trainer, for example, sets `DEVICES = (\"cuda\", \"cpu\")`: upstream trains under torchrun on CUDA only, and nothing in the native port needs CUDA."],[14810,"A training method is `[training.<id>]` in the engine's manifest (`TrainingMethod`). OmniVoice's LoRA:"],[12266,"A training run is one `train` job whose steps are its stages, each stage a child process; the stages are declared statically in the manifest"],[11341,"A training stage binds its policy process-wide (`dispatch.PROCESS_POLICY`), because autograd runs backward passes, and gradient checkpointing's recomputed forwards, on threads of its own."],[8690,"A training stage's process or a remote agent died or stopped answering"],[11204,"A training stage's process or a remote agent died or stopped answering; the engine raised an exception"],[12291,"A tunnel's or proxy's visitors must not browse the server's disk"],[12542,"A unit is a group of weights that moves together: a decoder