],[9316,"a voice's weights"],[16898,"a voice's weights"],[12724,"A warm time is the fastest warm run: the machine's other work only ever slows a run down. Comparisons that matter are interleaved, the two codes in separate processes, one after the other."],[8827,"A WAV of unknown length (PCM16 right after the header)"],[12580,"A weight that changes after placement goes through the handle (`handle.replace(module)`: a voice's own GPT-SoVITS weights), so a host copy is never stale."],[11507,"a whole patch per attention span and setting (`PatchDecoder`); the static caches kept with the model"],[15922,"a whole seeded request through Mizuoto's stack"],[16301,"About"],[13015,"About ×7: a token is 40 ms of audio, so the LM went from 1.7× slower than real time to 4× faster. The same tokens for three seeds (about 400 tokens each, to EOS) with and without graphs."],[15372,"About 10 GB of GPU memory to run the model whole (S2 Pro); on a CPU it runs in fp32 and is slow."],[9349,"about 100; Chinese"],[9335,"about 50 (Drama 3: 80+)"],[12588,"Above the manager, `RuntimeService` keeps at most `compute.max_resident_models` models loaded, unloads idle ones after `compute.unload_after_minutes` (server only), moves every idle model off a GPU before a fine-tune there (`release_device`), and after a job fails for running out of memory unloads every model not in use from every GPU (`ComputeService.release_after_oom`, ComfyUI's `unload_all_models`). See Runtime."],[11236,"Acceleration"],[14553,"Acceleration and speed work keep to the same tiers: an acceleration that changes bits (compilation, for one) stays at least within the engine's T1/T3 tolerance, with the measured error recorded; speed work on the default path must not change a bit."],[12278,"Accepting a licence is also required to download the weights and assets; the full text ships with the package and the command line can show it"],[8546,"Access control"],[8711,"Access control has three refusals of its own: `bad_host` (400), `bad_origin` (403) and `auth_required` (401)."],[9664,"Access token"],[10777,"Access token: once set, every API and socket request must carry it"],[10791,"Access tokens, the origin check and the Host check are described in HTTP API."],[16038,"Action"],[16500,"Action"],[11161,"Add `--help` at any level; a group name alone (such as `mizuoto model`) shows that group's help too. Every level accepts `--debug`."],[15029,"Add `keys.projects` to the lists invalidated on reconnect."],[10530,"Add a folder of clips in a known layout"],[10397,"Add a model folder from elsewhere (an earlier download, a fine-tune). When its file sizes match a catalogue model, it is checked by SHA-256 and imported as that model; otherwise it becomes a user model `<engine>/<name>`."],[10311,"Add a model's preset speaker to the library"],[10329,"Add a reference clip"],[10367,"Add a voice from a zip written by `voice export`"],[10267,"Add a voice from reference clips; missing transcripts come from speech recognition."],[8736,"Add a voice's fine-tuned weights from server paths"],[10533,"Add audio files or folders (a `.lab` or `.txt` beside a clip is its text), a voice's references or outputs"],[10497,"Add chapters and lines from a script; new speaker names join the cast"],[11677,"Add it to `EXPECTED_TREE` in `tests/cli/test_cli.py`. `test_command_tree` compares the whole tree, so a missing or extra command fails:"],[16757,"Add one or more reference clips: drop or choose files, **Record** (3 to 30 seconds of clear speech works best), **Server files** or **Earlier results**."],[10639,"Add or change a remote host and check that it answers; `address` is `host` or `host:port` (port 7870 by default)"],[10057,"Add or change: `{\"address\", \"token\", \"tls\", \"ca_file\"}`; a `null` token keeps the saved one"],[16527,"Add the audio to convert under **Recording**: drop or choose a file, **Record**, **Server files** or **Earlier results**."],[16535,"Add the audio to edit under **Recording**."],[10503,"Add, change or remove a speaker (a new id adds one)"],[16275,"Add, change or remove a speaker; a new id adds one, `''` clears a value"],[11549,"Adding a command"],[9927,"Adding a host"],[11547,"Adding a route"],[14936,"Adding a screen: Projects"],[14808,"Adding a trainer"],[12300,"Adding an engine"],[16550,"Adding clips"],[12011,"Adding things"],[11389,"additive bias; causal and local masks"],[8560,"Address"],[8955,"Address"],[10669,"Address to bind (`0.0.0.0`: every IPv4 interface; `::`: every interface, IPv4 and IPv6)"],[10761,"Address to bind; `0.0.0.0` for every interface"],[10623,"Address to listen on (default from settings: `127.0.0.1`; `0.0.0.0` for every interface)"],[9959,"Address to listen on; `0.0.0.0` for every interface"],[8541,"Addresses and documentation"],[12660,"Adds"],[13615,"After (per request, ms per second of audio)"],[11482,"After a capture the current stream waits for the capture stream: beginning a capture resets the generator's seed and offset tensors on the capture stream, and a first replay that overtook those kernels would draw from offset 0."],[14253,"After a load; when the model is unloaded (frees without copying back)"],[16466,"After a model change the screen picks a suitable way: the library voice you had chosen when it suits the new model, else a preset speaker, a description or a clip, in that order."],[12362,"After adding or changing a model, run `python scripts/dev.py model-manifests omnivoice`. `scripts/model_manifests.py` pins the Hugging Face revision to the current commit and lists every file with its size and SHA-256 (LFS files from their metadata, small files fetched and hashed) into `manifests/files/<manifest>`. Downloads verify against it; `test_catalogue_models_have_files_manifests` checks that every catalogue model has one."],[16675,"After confirming, runs every stage again from the first"],[9080,"After Hugging Face, also upload to ModelScope with `modelscope upload`"],[9833,"after that, allow a cheaper way for the step (tiled decoding,