ith `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the GPT wholly on its device, with a KV cache: IndexTTS 2/2.5, and 1.5 in fp16) the GPT-2's one-token steps of all beams run as graphs around each layer's attention; the cache, its beam reorder and the sampling stay eager. The same audio, 2.6–3.2 times faster per step on the 1.5's sizes. The beams' keys and values for every layer share one buffer (`BeamCaches`), which a step grows by a position with the beams' rows reordered in one copy per beam, each layer then writing its new key and value in place: each layer's keys and values are the contiguous tensors `index_select` and `torch.cat` made before, at half the copying (×1.11 on 30 s of speech). The graphs are captured per number of beams: until mizuoto-indextts 0.2.6 a one-beam request after a three-beam one replayed the three-beam graphs and failed."],[10995,"Beam search width for transcripts (2–10); 5 is what 0.1 used. More can be slightly more accurate and is slower. Transcripts are cached per width, so a change transcribes a clip again"],[8718,"Bearer header"],[180,"Bearer 头"],[12893,"before"],[12909,"before"],[12953,"before"],[13006,"before"],[13061,"before"],[13018,"Before"],[13032,"Before"],[13614,"Before (per request)"],[12807,"Before → after"],[14327,"Before each phase of a call, idle components on the same device give up memory, unit by unit, to make room; what does not fit streams from RAM (Memory)"],[13252,"before round 1 → round 1 (`8a021de`)"],[9192,"Behaviour"],[15925,"Behaviour is compared along with the audio: the parameters applied and the warnings, the voice mode chosen, the segments, the streamed chunks' lengths, the sample rate and the error codes of invalid requests."],[8993,"Being downloaded"],[16078,"Being downloaded; shows the amount done, the speed and the time left"],[16218,"Being rendered"],[16775,"below it, the clip's transcript; click **Save** (or press Enter) after changing it."],[16336,"Below them are this machine's devices, with each GPU's used and