no components; should one break with a future browser or Vue version, it is replaced inside `src/ui/` and feature code does not change."],[15745,"Both losses are transformers' `ForCausalLMLoss`, which shifts the already shifted labels once more; kept."],[15938,"Both were found while comparing E2-TTS: `F.linear` on a strided (non-contiguous) 3-D input takes another CPU kernel, with other rounding, when its weight requires grad, or when the weight is an *inference tensor* (made inside `torch.inference_mode()`), even under `no_grad`. Upstream's weights are ordinary parameters that require grad. So native engines leave parameters as `nn.Module` makes them (no `requires_grad_(False)`), and models are loaded outside inference mode; requests still run inside it."],[13190,"Bound by launches: GPT-SoVITS's GPT (about 56 %) and CosyVoice 2's language model (about 69 %)."],[13189,"Bound by the device's work (about 90 % busy or more): F5-TTS's DiT, IndexTTS's s2mel, BigVGAN and 1.5's GPT, CosyVoice 3's flow, Fish Speech's, Qwen3-TTS 1.7B's, VoxCPM's and OmniVoice's language models. (Capturing OmniVoice's step forward as a CUDA graph, tried in G2, gave 2 %.)"],[8727,"Bound with `--host 0.0.0.0`, the server logs that other machines can reach it, but it does not require a token. The API can delete files, download models and read audio on the server: set an access token, or put the server behind a firewall, a VPN or a reverse proxy with authentication."],[8732,"Browse and register audio files on the server"],[8743,"Browsed and registered paths must also lie inside `paths.browse_roots` (empty: the home folder, the data folder and every drive or volume). Remote clients upload instead: `PUT /audio/files`, or weights role by role with `PUT /voices/{id}/weights/{engine}/{role}`."],[14450,"Browser end-to-end tests (`tests/e2e`, below)"],[14398,"Build `mizuoto` (with the UI) and the gated engines' wheels into `dist/` (`scripts/build_wheels.py`)"],[8859,"Build a Mizuoto image from the repository's Dockerfile: its stages and build arguments, GPUs, volumes, the access token and environment variables, and the command line or an agent in a container."],[14152,"Build argument"],[16958,"Build argument"],[8861,"Build arguments"],[12419,"Build modules from `ops.default` (no random initialisation), load weights with `mizuoto.runtime.loading` (`load_state_dict`, `load_into`, strict), and leave parameters as `nn.Module` makes them. Draw every random number from `ctx.generator_for(device)` or `ctx.rng`, in upstream's order (see Runtime)."],[12383,"Build the model from `spec` (`model_id`, `model_dir`, `variant`, `device`, `dtype`, `options`) and return a `LoadedEngine`; report with `ctx.progress(\"loading:<part>\")`, check `ctx.check_cancel()` between parts"],[14212,"Builds the `Runtime` on first use, from the `compute` settings; says which engines are implemented here, what an engine is missing (`torch`, `mizuoto-fishspeech`…), its extras and its trainer"],[8879,"bun installs the locked dependencies; Node.js runs type checking and the web UI build (`mizuoto/webui/dist`)"],[341,"bun 按锁文件安装依赖，Node.js 执行类型检查和网页界面构建（`mizuoto/webui/dist`）"],[16442,"Button"],[16668,"Button"],[14961,"Button emphasis: at most one filled button per region (a view's main action, such as Speak or Train), tonal for secondary actions, outlined or text for the rest. Interactive elements have a visible focus indicator and, as a rule, a target of at least 48×48px (`dense` controls in compact rows and cards excepted)."],[9261,"By default only local names are accepted in `Host` (against DNS rebinding). Behind a tunnel or a reverse proxy, add the public name with `extra_hosts=[\"abc.example.com\"]` or `server.allow_host(\"https://abc.example.com\")`. Requests through such names are never treated as local, so the server-machine-only features (browsing server files and so on) are closed to them."],[12403,"Bytes of device memory a request needs beyond the weights; the model manager makes room for it"]