4325,"Components"],[12586,"Components in use by any request are never victims; the running model's components that the current phase does not need are. Each victim gives up units, in reverse fill order, until the shortfall is met (`partially_unload`); in `high` and `shared` it leaves whole. `empty_cache` runs after an eviction, and before a load whose device holds more unused cache than a quarter of its free memory (step 2 above); never per step."],[12514,"Components the phase does not name stay where they are and give up memory first when another phase needs it: an IndexTTS clone of a cached voice never places w2v-BERT or CAM++."],[47,"compute"],[8585,"compute"],[16294,"Compute"],[12420,"Compute attention with `mizuoto.runtime.accel.attention(q, k, v, site=SITE, …)`, never `F.scaled_dot_product_attention` (an architecture test forbids it): declare `SITE = accel.Site(\"<id>.<part>\")` once per call site, and pass the arguments upstream passed to SDPA (`causal` is its `is_causal`). A site where upstream wrote attention by hand gives that code as its `reference`; one that only its reference may compute is `swappable=False` (attentions with relative positions inside the scores are not sites at all: they stay hand-written). Where the site builds a mask from a structure (padding on one side, causal, a window), pass `mask_info` too, so faster kernels can take the call (Acceleration)."],[12682,"Conditions"],[12889,"Configuration"],[10696,"Configuration and environment variables"],[11234,"Configuration and environment variables: settings, environment variables and the data folder."],[11115,"Connect with TLS"],[11553,"Contents"],[16610,"Contents"],[17018,"Contents"],[12005,"Conventions"],[15040,"Conventions that hold everywhere"],[11629,"Conventions:"],[16522,"Convert voice"],[182,"Cookie"],[8720,"Cookie"],[14279,"Cooperative cancel. `check_cancel()` raises `Cancelled`, a `BaseException`, so model code's `except Exception` cannot swallow it. Engines call it at every token or ODE step"],[12571,"Copies are made outside inference mode, in the weights' own dtype, so a streamed layer computes with the same kind of tensor as a resident one (an inference tensor takes other CPU kernels). Each fetch checks for a cancel. A `Compiled` module above a streamed unit runs eagerly (its graph would hold the weights), and CUDA graphs are captured for models wholly on their device, or for a `sequence` handle whose streamed units rest in page-locked memory (`ModelHandle.graphable`; Qwen3-TTS's talker uses it). Captured, each streamed weight's copy is a memcpy node from its fixed host tensor into the graph's own memory, made inside the capture (a copy from the eager run before it is not used: the graph would keep reading that buffer after it is freed) and per leaf, so a layer split across graphs around its attention copies each weight once a step. The streamer counts the replays' copies (`ModelHandle.replayed`), so `meta.memory.streamed_mb` stays right."],[10874,"Copy streams for streamed weights (-1: two on NVIDIA and AMD, none elsewhere; 0: off); autoregressive models never prefetch"],[9827,"copy streams that move streamed weights while the GPU computes (`-1`: two on NVIDIA and AMD, none elsewhere); used for models that run once per input, not for autoregressive ones, where they only cost memory"],[11637,"Core method"],[14548,"Corpus runs in each engine's production dtype and device, native against reference; seeds not aligned (GPU kernels differ)"],[10335,"Correct a clip's transcript"],[10545,"Correct, exclude or delete a clip"],[14538,"Cosine ≥ 0.999"],[734,"CosyVoice"],[1327,"CosyVoice"],[2911,"CosyVoice"],[5410,"CosyVoice"],[6317,"CosyVoice"],[6613,"CosyVoice"],[7335,"CosyVoice"],[7568,"CosyVoice"],[8348,"CosyVoice"],[9272,"CosyVoice"],[9865,"CosyVoice"],[11449,"CosyVoice"],[13948,"CosyVoice"],[14855,"CosyVoice"],[15151,"CosyVoice"],[15873,"CosyVoice"],[16106,"CosyVoice"],[16885,"CosyVoice"],[9297,"CosyVoice (`cosyvoice`)"],[16590,"CosyVoice (300M, 2