ndexTTS，采用 bilibili Model Use License"],[12803,"IndexTTS: GPT-2's GELU in place; a beam reorder that keeps every row skipped"],[4265,"IndexTTS：GPT-2 的 GELU 原地计算；跳过保留所有行的 beam 重排"],[15561,"IndexTTS's Conformer and the perceiver resampler"],[801,"IndexTTS（`indextts`）"],[2973,"IndexTTS（`mizuoto_indextts/gpt.py`）"],[11463,"Inductor caches its code in `/tmp/torchinductor_<user>`. The Docker image has no C compiler, so it runs eagerly there."],[2925,"Inductor 把生成的代码缓存在 `/tmp/torchinductor_<user>`。Docker 镜像中没有 C 编译器，所以在那里按即时执行运行。"],[11895,"Inference and training on that device; a job waiting for it can be **run anyway** (`run_anyway`)"],[12805,"Inference, warm request (s), every case identical to before:"],[8662,"Input that does not validate; a path outside its allowed root"],[17046,"Install Mizuoto"],[14350,"Install Mizuoto editable, with the development tools"],[14400,"Install the built wheels over a CPU torch in a new environment and try them (`scripts/smoke_wheels.py`)"],[17039,"Install the new version the same way, for example `pip install --upgrade mizuoto` (with `mizuoto-fishspeech mizuoto-indextts` if you use them, so pip picks the versions that work with the new Mizuoto); from source, `git pull`, run the install command again and rebuild the UI. With Docker, rebuild the image; the `/data` volume stays."],[14404,"Install the UI's dependencies / build the UI / Vite only (expects a running API)"],[14349,"Install torch first"],[16926,"Installation"],[9938,"Installed models (`mizuoto model download`)"],[11866,"Installed models, voices, datasets, experiments and projects are folders with JSON sidecars (`model.json`, `voice.json`, `dataset.json`, `experiment.json`, `project.json`), not rows: nothing queries them, and a folder scan cannot drift from the files. The database (`mizuoto/core/db/database.py`: one shared connection, WAL mode, `PRAGMA user_version` counting the migrations run, migrations append-only) keeps what is queried: jobs (with their request JSON and owning process id), outputs (with applied parameters, timings and licence tags), audio files, transcripts, presets and client state."],[11313,"Installed packages from their metadata and install commands that keep torch (standard library only)"],[16950,"Installing reaches PyPI and the PyTorch download site; downloading models reaches Hugging Face, hf-mirror or ModelScope (chosen in **Settings › Downloads**)"],[8760,"Instead of polling, follow `job_updated` among the events."],[14105,"Intel (XPU)"],[5567,"Intel（XPU）"],[8563,"Interactive documentation (Swagger UI)"],[16791,"Interface overview"],[3582,"InvokeAI"],[12120,"InvokeAI"],[3573,"InvokeAI 的前后端结构是这个骨架的出发点。采用的部分："],[12111,"InvokeAI's front-end/back-end structure is where the skeleton started. What was taken:"],[9875,"It applies to models loaded after the change; loaded models keep what they had."],[12239,"It covers every code path (`layer.forward_step`, `vae.decode`, custom layers), and costs nothing while a model is whole on its device"],[12141,"It creates a listening socket and binds it to the configured host and port; on `EADDRINUSE` or `EACCES` (which covers Windows' excluded port ranges) it tries the next port, up to 20 attempts and never past 65535, and fails with a clear error when none is free. `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE` on Windows, `SO_REUSEADDR` elsewhere."],[14454,"It declares **every** capability: preset speakers, cloning, design, style and emotion, streamed output and streamed text input, voice conversion, speech editing, batches, weights, a `transcribe` op (so the ASR path is testable too), training."],[16212,"It has a take, but its text, speaker, the speaker's model, voice or parameters changed since, or the library voice it uses was changed"],[16210,"It has a take, made from its current text and settings"],[9906,"it has no seed (a batch draws random numbers differently from a single request);"],[9683,"It holds `settings.toml`, the database `mizuoto.db`, `models/`, `voices/`, `outputs/`, `datasets/`, `experiments/`, `projects/`, `cache/`, `jobs/` (job logs) and `logs/`."],[16169,"It imports as one chapter of six lines: \"Anna\" and \"Old man\" each begin two lines and become two new speakers; the other lines are the narrator's; the first line, the dialogue and the last line are three paragraphs."],[9028,"It is not pinned to a commit, but each file is checked against the manifest's size and SHA-256 like any other; a file that does not match comes from the official repository."],[9907,"it is not streamed text input;"],[16151,"It means"],[14884,"It moves the real stdout aside for events and points file descriptor 1 at stderr, so whatever libraries print goes to the log, not into the event stream. Events are JSON lines prefixed with `@mizuoto ` (`mizuoto/core/jobs/jsonl.py`), and records of the `mizuoto` loggers become `LogEvent`s."],[9880,"It needs a working C++ compiler. Without one, or when a model's code cannot be compiled, Mizuoto logs one warning and runs that model as before. The Docker image has none, so there it changes nothing."],[9067,"It reads `MIRROR.json` (from `build` or `mirror_fetch.py`) and writes:"],[9103,"It sends a HEAD request to each catalogue file's URL, the one Mizuoto itself would download, and prints `complete` or the number of missing files per model; the exit code is 1 when anything is missing."],[14414,"It starts the API as `python -m mizuoto webui --no-open --port 7869 --strict-port` (with the repository root on `PYTHONPATH`) and Vite as `bun run dev`, passing `MIZUOTO_BACKEND=http://127.0.0.1:7869` to Vite. Vite proxies `/api` and `/ws` to the API, so the browser only opens `http://localhost:5173`. UI changes reload in place; Python changes, an engine's included, need the task restarted (models load into the server's process). While the API is down, Vite's proxy prints one short line every few seconds instead of a flood of connection errors."],[11461,"It traces with its policy's `trace_run` (a compiled graph cannot read a context variable), one compiled call at a time while a policy other than `auto` is active."],[14136,"It tries the built distributions as a user gets them. In a temporary folder outside the checkout, uv creates a new environment (`--python`, 3.11 by default), installs torch first from `--torch-index` (the CPU build by default; `--torch` picks the version, `torch>=2.8` by default), then, in one install, the wheels in `--dist` and the distributions it lacks from `--index` (`--others index`, the default), which must leave that torch in place. Since each distribution is released on its own, a release is tried with the others as users have them: a `mizuoto` wheel with the gated engines' released packages, a gated engine's wheel with the newest released Mizuoto its range allows. A Mizuoto release the released gated packages do not allow fails here. The installed versions must be the wheels'. uv runs without the machine's configuration (`--no-config`, no `UV_*`/`PIP_*` variables). Then, in a temporary data folder:"],[14453,"It turns each character into a short tone whose pitch comes from the voice (a preset, a description, the references' SHA-256 or a hash of the weights), so different voices sound different, and draws from `ctx.rng`, so the same seed gives the same audio."],[16190,"Item"],[16937,"Item"],[12243,"Its blocks run through `prompt` / `step`, which read the fused projections directly; the model is 150 MB"],[11419,"its constraints refuse the call (device, capability, dtype, head dim, mask, causal over unequal lengths, scale);"],[13406,"its CUDA graphs are off while compiling"],[11458,"its decoding steps' small operations, inside its CUDA graphs (below)"],[13377,"its export does not repeat"],[11416,"its probe says it cannot run on the device (not installed, wrong version, no kernels, self-test failed);"],[16047,"Its spectrogram (a voice's high-frequency cut-off, noise, clicks) and pitch curve (octave jumps, monotone stretches), with its format, median pitch and how much of it is voiced; computed on the server once, then cached"],[16509,"Its spectrogram (a voice's high-frequency cut-off, noise, clicks) and pitch curve (octave jumps, monotone stretches), with its format, median pitch and how much of it is voiced; computed on the server once, then cached"],[16654,"its text (labelled with the speaker; without text it says **No text: transcribe it or type it**); save with the save button or Enter;"],[9905,"its text is one segment (not split, not a batch request);"],[15515,"Japanese and Korean text need their extras; without them such text fails with `capability_not_supported` and the install command in the hint. pyopenjtalk 0.4.1 is a source package that needs CMake and a C++ compiler."],[15543,"Japanese and Spanish, a language token, and a speed (`duration_factor = 1 / speed`)"],[15496,"Japanese needs `pyopenjtalk==0.4.1` (extra `mizuoto[gptsovits-ja]`): pyopenjtalk-plus changes OpenJTalk's rules, and 18 % of Japanese sentences came out differently with it. Korean needs MeCab-ko and jamo (extra `mizuoto[gptsovits-ko]`). The Japanese user dictionary is compiled once into the `gptsovits/open-jtalk` asset's `.mizuoto/` folder."],[12196,"Japanese through `pyopenjtalk==0.4.1`, not pyopenjtalk-plus; Simplified → Traditional through the C++ `opencc==1.4.2`; Chinese segmentation through `jieba` instead of `jieba_fast`"],[15492,"jieba replaces jieba_fast (the same dictionary; identical on 20 446 texts);"],[6954,"jieba 替代 jieba_fast（同一词典；在 20 446 条文本上结果相同）；"],[14086,"jieba_fast, g2p_en, nltk (and the data it downloads at run time)"],[5548,"jieba_fast、g2p_en、nltk（以及它运行时下载的数据）"],[14087,"jieba; the ported GRU and tagger, with their data shipped"],[5549,"jieba；移植的 GRU 与词性标注器，数据随包发布"],[14764,"Job"],[17035,"Job logs and server logs"],[89,"jobs"],[8627,"jobs"],[8548,"Jobs"],[8629,"Jobs"],[11811,"Jobs"],[11695,"Jobs and named resources"],[9687,"Jobs go into the same database, so the web UI's **Jobs** panel and `mizuoto job list` show both sides' jobs."],[12090,"Jobs