nt` (as `ProjectView.vue`'s draft does)."],[10472,"List presets"],[10488,"List projects"],[10542,"List the clips and their texts"],[10421,"List the GPUs found (NVIDIA, AMD, Intel, Apple) and how they were found; check torch against them and print the command that installs the right build; list each engine as available or missing (with what it lacks: torch, `mizuoto-fishspeech`, `mizuoto-indextts`) and the optional extras not installed; and, per engine, which installed models load whole on each GPU and which only partly (the rest of their weights streaming from RAM, slower), under the memory settings in effect. Exits with code 1 when a check fails."],[10428,"List the loaded models (device, memory, last use, busy or idle), and unload them. The models live in the server's process: with a server running (`mizuoto webui`), the command asks it (through `server.json` in the data folder); otherwise its own process has nothing loaded."],[16287,"List the projects"],[9979,"Listening beyond this machine without TLS, the agent warns:"],[9929,"Listing and removing"],[12253,"Listing devices or serving the UI should not pay a torch import of a second or two"],[8081,"LJSpeech 格式"],[9302,"LLM, LLM + flow"],[16888,"LLM, LLM + flow"],[764,"LLM、LLM + flow"],[8351,"LLM、LLM + flow"],[11283,"load option `attention_span` (off)"],[11280,"load option `fused_projections` (off)"],[13536,"Load s, before → after"],[16515,"Load the model, voice, text and parameters that made it back into Speak"],[9746,"Loaded models and memory"],[8544,"Loaded models and the doctor"],[12166,"Loading and detection (safetensors or `weights_only` pickles, key renaming)"],[12574,"Loading never holds a float32 copy of a model that runs in half precision: an engine casts the model before it copies the checkpoint in, the same values as loading in float32 and casting after. Qwen3-TTS 1.7B's load fell from 7.4 to 4.2 GB of RAM (11.1 to 5.5 GB resident, host copies off, 2026-10-19); F5-TTS, VoxCPM, Fish Speech and OmniVoice load this way too. The cast is `loading.cast`: `Module.to(dtype)` (through `_apply`, so a module's own `_apply` still decides, such as `Rotary` keeping `inv_freq` float32), except that a tensor the checkpoint will fill gets new, unwritten memory instead of a copy of its unwritten values. `Module.to` wrote a whole copy of the model in RAM that the checkpoint then replaced: the peak of a load whose weights stay in the file (Fish S2 Pro: 9 GB, now 1.6)."],[12700,"Loading without a RAM copy (G10)"],[14907,"Loads the engine's own implementation in the stage process (a private `Runtime` whose manager places weights as the host's would: the host's `compute` settings from the request, and its calibrated working-memory estimates, read but not written back; each preview runs in an export stage, a process of its own, so no optimizer state or gradients are on the device) and speaks `text` with the new weights (`weights` on the base model) or the new model (`model_dir`) under seed 1234, kept as a sample. A failure is only a warning, never a failed stage; skipped when `training.previews` is off"],[16201,"Loads the line's whole request (model, voice, text, parameters) into Speak, to try things out"],[13952,"local DiT"],[14199,"LocalEngine: calling a model in this process"],[5661,"LocalEngine：在本进程中调用模型"],[9676,"Location"],[9728,"Location"],[10722,"Location"],[8750,"Log"],[9727,"Log"],[10745,"Log level: `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING` or `ERROR` (default `INFO`)"],[9670,"Logs"],[8919,"Logs reach `docker logs` at once"],[8744,"Long operations (synthesis, downloads, training, project renders…) return a job rather than waiting for it:"],[11798,"Long-form projects: cast, chapters, lines and takes"],[12430,"Look at random numbers first: upstream may draw them while building a model or preparing a reference (HuBERT's layer drop, IndexTTS's w2v-BERT, CosyVoice 3's vocoder noise), or with tensors of other strides. Then at tensor shapes and kernels: SDPA with or without a mask, a mask's dtype, contiguity, the CPU thread count. `AGENTS.md` §2b lists such findings engine by engine."],[9337,"LoRA (S2 Pro)"],[16913,"LoRA (S2 Pro)"],[799,"LoRA（S2 Pro）"],[8376,"LoRA（S2 Pro）"],[13414,"Losses"],[16557,"Losses"],[12209,"Losses, learning rates and exported weights then match upstream byte for byte, and the exports load in both implementations"],[14680,"Loudness and F0 stay inside the reference's interquartile range for every voice of every set. The one systematic difference within tolerance is IndexTTS 1.5's UTMOS, 0.03 lower (p 0.025, mostly the second English voice), the model whose GPU output already differed from 0.1's with the same seed (2.3 dB, G0 on Performance); its causes have since been found and fixed (IndexTTS). Fish Speech S2 Pro has no reference on a GPU (0.1's cloning fails there): native alone, 1.23 % error, no failed clip, similarity 0.723, UTMOS 4.07. **Opt-ins that change audio** are judged the same way: the native run with the opt-in (`--setting`, or `--option` for a request option) against the default native run, on the sets each one changes. Every one passes (default → opt-in):"],[16687,"Low"],[16688,"Lowest"],[6411,"M3 的窗口尺寸分级：compact（\\< 600px）、medium（\\< 840px）、expanded（\\< 1200px）、large（\\< 1600px）、extra-large"],[14949,"M3's window size classes: compact (\\< 600px), medium (\\< 840px), expanded (\\< 1200px), large (\\< 1600px), extra-large"],[1141,"macOS"],[2187,"macOS"],[8476,"macOS"],[9679,"macOS"],[10725,"macOS"],[17013,"macOS"],[5570,"macOS arm64"],[14108,"macOS arm64"],[9457,"Main capabilities"],[9628,"Main capabilities"],[10486,"Main options"],[10519,"Main options"],[10553,"Main options"],[8577,"Main routes"],[8946,"Maintaining a mirror"],[10481,"Make a preset its model's default"],[14281,"Makes the context the running thread's request; layers then call the module-level `check_cancel()` without being handed it"],[9005,"Manage them on their own in **Models** › **Shared files**, or:"],[10131,"Many commands also take `--json`, which print