.1 on the CPU in fp32 for cloning, design, its own voice and the fine-tuned model) and what exactness took."],[11285,"OmniVoice's packed guidance"],[12638,"OmniVoice's tokenizer"],[14807,"OmniVoice's trainer, as an example"],[780,"OmniVoice（`omnivoice`）"],[5070,"OmniVoice（bf16）"],[9829,"on"],[16358,"on"],[16370,"on"],[16385,"on"],[16397,"on"],[16626,"on"],[16629,"on"],[16632,"on"],[15997,"On **Speak**, a model that is not downloaded yet replaces the **Speak** button with the one that downloads it. Downloads are jobs, so you can leave the page at any time."],[16003,"On **Speak**, a model whose engine is not available replaces the button at the bottom with the command that installs what it needs. The command line:"],[16011,"On **Speak**, after choosing a model, the button at the bottom offers **Download** *model* *(size)*."],[8726,"On a 401 the web UI shows the **Access token** dialog and asks for it once."],[9753,"On a CPU"],[9877,"On a CPU (fp32, 8 threads) the compiled module's time dropped by 23 % for F5-TTS (a whole request from 60 s to 45 s), 7 % for IndexTTS's DiT and 20 % for its BigVGAN, 7 % for GPT-SoVITS v4, and nothing for CosyVoice or (bf16) VoxCPM. The audio differs slightly from the uncompiled run; for VoxCPM that can move where the speech ends."],[15363,"On a free RTX 3060 the whole model's frame takes about 64 ms with graphs. About 50 ms of that is reading 16 GB of weights at close to the card's bandwidth; most of the rest is thousands of small kernels. `compute.compile` (opt-in, not exact; `fused.py`) fuses them: it compiles each layer's halves around its attention, the attention over the cache, the step's embeddings and heads, and the draws' probabilities, inside the same graphs, with the eager code untouched when it is off. Each frame is then 1.15 times faster. The draws are unchanged, but the probabilities differ in their last bits, so the speech is another take of the same text and voice, which still repeats under a seed and passes the contract suite. It runs only while the model is wholly on its device, and the output lists it (`applied[\"compile\"]`). Details: Acceleration."],[15612,"On a GPU (an RTX 3090, 2026-10-19, against 0.1 in each version's own precision) all four cases are identical sample for sample: 1.5 in fp16 (2.3 dB before the fixes above), the two IndexTTS-2 cases and 2.5 in bf16 (−2.6 dB before its padding masks). The only difference reported is the `cuda_graphs` label: the graphs replay the same kernels."],[15250,"On a GPU (an RTX 3090, 2026-10-19, stage by stage against upstream on torch 2.8): with upstream's CAM++ embedding fed to Mizuoto, the v2 and v3 English clones are identical sample for sample; that took HiFT's weight norm folded on the device in the F0 predictor's dtype (upstream computes it there at every call). Each side making its own embedding, the v2 clone is identical too (its flow absorbs CAM++'s 5e-7) and v3 is at 14.2 dB, which is CAM++'s noise as on the CPU. Upstream on its own torch 2.3.1 (cuDNN 8.9) differs from itself on torch 2.8 at the first convolution, so the comparison takes 2.8."],[15750,"On a GPU (an RTX 3090, bf16, 2026-10-19, against 0.1) all eight cases are identical sample for sample too. That took four things upstream does: RoPE's `inv_freq` kept in float32 when the model is cast to bf16 (`from_pretrained(dtype=…)` leaves the buffer it built in float32; a rounded one turned late positions by other angles), the speech tokenizer's encoder and decoder given transformers' boolean causal mask instead of `is_causal` (transformers 4.57's packed-sequence check keeps the mask whenever position ids come without a padding mask or a cache, and on a GPU the two pick other kernels), the encoder's q, k and v made contiguous as transformers makes them, and q and k normed apart (above). Against the code before, the talker costs ×0.92–0.96 on that GPU (rounds `g6-before`, `g6-after`)."],[15673,"On a GPU (an RTX 3090, bf16, 2026-10-19, against 0.1) the four cases are identical sample for sample too, once the shared Qwen decoder kept RoPE's `inv_freq` in float32 through the cast to bf16 and normed q and k apart, as transformers does (see Qwen3-TTS); speed unchanged (×1.01)."],[15514,"On a GPU (an RTX 3090, fp16, 2026-10-19, stage by stage against 0.1): the codes, HuBERT, the text and style encoders are identical; v2 and v4 differ from 0.1 only by upstream's TorchScript WaveNet gate (`commons.fused_add_tanh_sigmoid_multiply`), which CUDA's fuser compiles after its first calls, so its bits depend on the shapes the process has already seen. With the gate scripted as upstream's (an experiment) both cases are identical sample for sample to 0.1; Mizuoto keeps the gate eager (v2 48.9 dB, v4 32.4 dB), for the reason VoxCPM's Snake runs eagerly (VoxCPM): every request then gives the same bits. The T4 tier judges the two equivalent."],[9878,"On a GPU (RTX 3090) the warm requests were 1.34× faster for F5-TTS, 1.14× for GPT-SoVITS v4 and 1.03–1.06× for IndexTTS and CosyVoice, after 55–134 s of compiling; VoxCPM runs without its CUDA graphs while compiled and was slower (0.41–0.64×): leave it off for VoxCPM."],[15309,"On a GPU the model runs in fp16 as upstream does; Mizuoto offers no fp32 rotary embedding there."],[9106,"On a machine with the models downloaded, build the mirror under `<repo id>/resolve/main`:"],[14997,"On connect and reconnect the active jobs are fetched again (`resync()`); a reconnect also invalidates the usual lists on screen."],[15837,"On CUDA the first request in a process decodes its latents (which are identical) with slightly different bits from later requests; later requests repeat each other exactly."],[14487,"On CUDA, unloading the model after a request leaves at most 64 MB more allocated than before it loaded (8 MB of cuBLAS workspace in practice)"],[12046,"On GPUs in reduced precision, bit identity is not required; modules are judged by their error and whole runs statistically. The tiers and tolerances are in Testing."],[9977,"On its first start without a token the agent makes a random one, saves it as `remote.agent.token` and prints it:"],[12211,"On its own torch 2.3.1 and on 2.8, sampling already diverges"],[16600,"On the **Datasets** tab, click **New dataset**."],[16658,"On the **Experiments** tab, click **New experiment** (or **Train on it** on a dataset's page)."],[9934,"On the agent"],[12694,"On the CPU"],[14017,"On the CPU (the 13 cases of the CPU rounds, a Ryzen 9 5900X shared with another workload, the same two builds alternated, two rounds each): all 39 comparisons identical; the warm runs differ by −7.2 to +5.0 % in both directions, −0.4 % on average, within that machine's spread (the base build's own two rounds differ by up to 12 %). On the CPU nothing streams, so nothing new runs there but the storage check in `host_bytes`."],[14263,"On the CPU nothing is moved and nothing is counted, unless `DeviceService(simulate={\"cpu\": bytes})` makes it play a GPU (tests and the parity harness: `compute.simulate_vram_mb`)."],[12516,"On the CPU the manager moves and counts nothing (the load and offload device are the same), so phases cost nothing there."],[14495,"On the CPU, every catalogue model of every engine passes the contract suite. On an RTX 3090 (2026-10-19) every installed model passed the four tests above, the licence-gated ones included: the first audio after 0.1–2.3 s of 0.9–6 s requests, cancelled in 0.05–0.6 s, and at most 8 MB left on the device after unloading. The whole suite takes hours (the larger the model, the slower), so when changing one engine, run that engine."],[15418,"On the CPU, in float32 with 16 threads, a frame takes about 2.1 s, upstream's modules as long (a second of speech is 21.5 frames: some 45 s of compute); a prompt of 230 rows about 35 s. On a GPU it needs about 44 GB to hold the whole model, or its experts (30 GiB) stream from RAM; where RAM cannot hold them either, the layers' experts that do not fit are kept in files (`runtime.filemap`, Memory). First run on a GPU, 2026-11-05: an RTX 3060 (12 GB, PCIe x4) in a machine with 31 GB of RAM, bf16: 9.1 GB on the GPU, 17.0 GB of experts in page-locked RAM, 20.7 GB in files; a warm request of 5.5–8.3 s of speech took 128–162 s (176–226 GB copied to the GPU a request, 1.4 GB/s), its two runs identical; 15–32 GiB of it read from the disk, the rest of the file-backed experts from the page cache (72–87 %); RAM never fell below 7.9 GB available."],[15397,"On the CPU, upstream's modules and the port give the same hidden states, logits, frames and audio, bit for bit and sample for sample (see Parity). In particular:"],[9935,"On the host"],[9110,"On the other machines:"],[9262,"Once it is reachable, anyone with the address can use it: set `access_token`, or add authentication of your own. HTTP API details the access checks."],[9263,"Once started, the server writes `server.json` (`host`, `port`, `url`, `pid`) into the data folder so other programs can find it; `stop()` removes it."],[16022,"Once the model is downloaded, open **Speak**, choose it and a voice, type some text and click **Speak**. Speak explains every option."],[16647,"Once there are clips, the **Report** shows:"],[12599,"one 30 s window at a time"],[16620,"One audio file name and its text per line"],[16096,"One card per engine:"],[12489,"One component: whole or partly placed, host copies, hooks for streamed units"],[12200,"One Docker image holds the server, the UI and every engine; the licence-gated engines come with `GATED=1`"],[14218,"One engine on one device in this process, and the handle of one of its loaded models"],[11771,"One engine per (engine, device), here or on a remote host; `loaded()` gives a model's `EngineHandle`; unloading, the idle reaper, the doctor"],[14215,"One engine per (engine, device), made on demand; `loaded()` gives a model's `EngineHandle`; `max_resident_models`, the idle reaper, `runtime_changed`, the doctor"],[12108,"One environment, every engine implemented in-tree on a ComfyUI-style runtime"],[15038,"One environment, one process"],[8925,"One GPU only: `--gpus '\"device=1\"'`."],[16957,"One image holds the server, the UI and every engine, with GPT-SoVITS's Japanese and Korean front ends; models go to the `/data` volume."],[12386,"One loaded model. It is not re-entrant: the job scheduler gives it one request at a time (the `engine:<engine>:<device>` resource)."],[14901,"One loss point"],[14875,"One more rule: when a stage is **run again**, the finished stages after it that were not part of the same run lose their fingerprints. They read the old stage's files, so they are stale even when the inputs (and fingerprints) are the same."],[11678,"One name cannot be both a command and a group, so the environment variable listing is `mizuoto env vars`, not `mizuoto env`."],[16461,"One of the model's own speakers (Qwen3-TTS CustomVoice, CosyVoice 300M SFT…)"],[11683,"One operation, one core method"],[12127,"One optional access token (a Bearer header, the `mizuoto_token` cookie or `?token=`), plus a Host check (against DNS rebinding) and an Origin check on state-changing requests; binding to a non-loopback address logs a warning"],[16747,"One or more reference clips with their transcripts, for cloning"],[10176,"One output per line of the text"],[14233,"One per call: cancel, generators, progress, text pieces, scratch"],[12492,"One per device: the device copies of streamed units, their learnt order, prefetch on side streams, pinning"],[16407,"One per line. Dialogs such as **Server files** and **Import a model folder** browse only these. **Empty: your home folder, the data folder and every drive.**"],[15119,"One phase per transcription: the whole model, the decoder marked `hot` (it runs per token and beam), `kind=\"sequence\"`. With `compute.oom_fallback`, a transcription that runs out of memory decodes one 30 s window at a time instead of four; that is another batch shape, so in rare ties a transcript may differ."],[12105,"One Python environment and one worker process per engine, upstream code vendored as it was"],[12182,"One Python environment, every engine ported in-tree and run in the server's own process; no upstream code vendored"],[11555,"One router module per resource, `routers/<resource>.py`, each with `APIRouter(prefix=\"/v1/<resource>\")`"],[16183,"One row per line, from left to right:"],[16072,"One row per model, with its name, variant, size, GPU memory (**N GB of GPU memory**) and description, and its state:"],[12273,"One synthesis path serves every feature, so micro-batching and every engine come for free"],[11855,"One TCP connection (optionally TLS) is a session for one (engine, device): `open`, `load`, `prepare_voice`, `synthesize`, `convert`, `edit`, `call`, `unload`, `status` one after another; `cancel` and `text` at any time. Frames are length-prefixed JSON or binary (`core/remote/frames.py`, standard library only)."],[14458,"One temporary data folder per test and an empty environment (`environ={}`: the developer's own `MIZUOTO_*` variables never leak in)."],[12601,"one text at a time"],[15627,"One variant, `v0` (catalogue model `omnivoice/omnivoice`): cloning (the transcript is required; Mizuoto supplies it by speech recognition when it is missing, so the engine never loads Whisper itself), design from a closed vocabulary of attributes, the model's own voice, and 13 inline non-verbal tags."],[15093,"One variant, `whisper` (catalogue model `asr/whisper-large-v3-turbo`); the model is built from `config.json`, so other Whisper sizes in the same format load too. The folder holds `config.json`, `generation_config.json`, `model.safetensors` (or `pytorch_model.bin`), `preprocessor_config.json`, `tokenizer.json` and `tokenizer_config.json`."],[10753,"Only `MIZUOTO_*` variables whose names contain `__` are overrides."],[14964,"Only components under `ui/` (plus `theme/tokens.css` and the tests' `test/setup.ts`) import `@material/web`. Views and feature components import `AppButton`, `TextField`, `AppDialog`, `SegmentedButton`, `Stepper`, `LineChart`… from `@/ui`."],[16507,"Only in a browser on the server machine"],[12240,"Only linear and convolution weights stream, never embeddings"],[16636,"Only longer clips are cut"],[12354,"Only names from `CommonParam` (`temperature`, `top_p`, `num_steps`, `speed`, `seed`…). `target` is the engine's own name; `default` only shows the engine's default, Mizuoto never imposes it; `approximate = true` adds a warning to results; `variants` and `streaming` narrow where it applies"],[12270,"Only requests that differ in nothing but their text, with one segment and no seed, join a micro-batch"],[15298,"Only the Vocos vocoder is offered; upstream's BigVGAN variant of the v0 model is not in the catalogue."],[9053,"Only these models and shared files"],[9036,"Only these models and shared files (default: every installed one)"],[10425,"Only this engine (default: all)"],[10264,"Only voices in this language (`list`)"],[12532,"only when the weights take at most half of the device's memory (`low_ratio`)"],[5539,"ONNX 文件里的权重由仓库内的协议缓冲区读取器（`runtime/convert/onnx.py`）转换成 torch 模块，转换结果缓存在模型文件夹的 `.mizuoto/` 下"],[5538,"onnxruntime"],[14076,"onnxruntime"],[16014,"Open **Models › Engines** and click **Accept the licence** on the engine's card (or, on **Speak** with one of its models chosen, **Accept the** *engine* **licence** at the bottom)."],[16142,"Open **Projects** in the navigation. Each card shows the project's name, rendered lines out of all lines (red when some failed), its description, **N chapter(s) · N line(s)**, **N speaker(s)**, the length of what is rendered and a bar coloured by the lines' states. Click a card to open the project."],[17062,"Open **Speak** in the navigation (the UI starts there)."],[9227,"Open a browser once started"],[10773,"Open a browser when `mizuoto webui` starts"],[11232,"Open a new terminal afterwards to complete commands, subcommands and options."],[16045,"Open its folder on the server (only in a browser on the server machine)"],[16053,"Open Speak with the model, voice, text and parameters that made it (the same seed when one was set); for results of a synthesis"],[16049,"Open Speak with this result as **A clip**, its text as the transcript"],[16835,"Open text-to-speech engines in one platform: one web UI, one command line and one HTTP API."],[17068,"Open the **Model** picker and choose a real model, for example **Qwen3-TTS 1.7B CustomVoice**. Models that are not ready carry badges such as **Not downloaded** or **Not available**, but can still be chosen."],[10678,"Open the web UI in a browser"],[16998,"Open the web UI in a browser or not"],[8556,"OpenAI-compatible API"],[8571,"OpenAI-compatible API"],[14078,"openai-whisper, faster-whisper (CTranslate2)"],[5540,"openai-whisper、faster-whisper（CTranslate2）"],[8565,"OpenAPI schema"],[11545,"OpenAPI with events"],[3007,"OpenAPI 与事件"],[27,"OpenAPI 结构"],[36,"OpenAPI 结构里也列出了 socket 推送的事件类型，可以用它生成客户端类型。"],[1019,"OpenBMB 的无离散分词语音合成：逐个“块”（patch）生成连续的语音潜变量（由 MiniCPM-4 语言模型和每块一个小扩散模型完成），中间没有语音编码。适合：自然的音色克隆（有无参考文本均可）、用一句描述生成音色、对克隆的音色加风格指令，以及 30 种语言的 48 kHz 合成（VoxCPM2）。"],[7225,"OpenBMB 的无离散分词语音合成（OpenBMB/VoxCPM，Apache-2.0，代码与权重）：逐块（patch）生成连续的语音潜变量，中间没有离散编码。代码：`mizuoto/engines/voxcpm`。Mizuoto 0.1 没有 VoxCPM，所以参考实现是上游自己的包，在同一个 Mizuoto 完整链路中经适配器运行，库版本与上游锁定的一致（transformers 5.3.0、tokenizers 0.22.2、wetext 0.1.2、inflect 7.5.0）。在 CPU 上以相同种子运行时，每个组件和每个请求在 bf16（上游的默认）和 fp32 下都与它完全相同，两个训练器得到的权重也逐位相同。面向用户的说明见引擎详解。"],[15763,"OpenBMB's tokenizer-free TTS (OpenBMB/VoxCPM, Apache-2.0, code and weights): continuous speech latents generated patch by patch, with no discrete codes. Code: `mizuoto/engines/voxcpm`. Mizuoto 0.1 had no VoxCPM, so the reference is upstream's own package, run behind an adapter in the same Mizuoto stack with the library versions upstream locks (transformers 5.3.0, tokenizers 0.22.2, wetext 0.1.2, inflect 7.5.0). On the CPU with the same seed every component and request is identical to it in bf16 (upstream's default) and in fp32, and both trainers give its weights bit for bit. User-facing details: Engines in depth."],[9557,"OpenBMB's tokenizer-free TTS: it generates continuous speech latents patch by patch (a MiniCPM-4 language model and a small diffusion model per patch), with no speech codes in between. Best for: natural cloning, with or without the clip's transcript; voices made from a sentence of description; style instructions on a cloned voice; 30 languages at 48 kHz (VoxCPM2)."],[15493,"OpenCC is the C++ `opencc==1.4.2` (the pure-Python port differs on 321 of 182 814 conversions, which feed G2PW);"],[6955,"OpenCC 用 C++ 版 `opencc==1.4.2`（纯 Python 移植版在 182 814 次转换中有 321 次不同，而这些结果会送入 G2PW）；"],[9116,"Opening the services"],[11530,"OpenMP threads bound to distinct physical cores (`OMP_PLACES=cores`, `OMP_PROC_BIND=close`). Left to the scheduler two threads sometimes share a core, and that process runs a third slower for its whole life. `off` leaves placement to the scheduler (better when other busy programs share the cores)"],[16939,"Operating system"],[8746,"Operation"],[12401,"Operations named in the manifest's `ops` (ASR's `transcribe`, Fish Speech's `codec_encode` / `codec_decode`)"],[14681,"Opt-in"],[9072,"Option"],[9085,"Option"],[9952,"Option"],[10123,"Option"],[10257,"Option"],[10341,"Option"],[10620,"Option"],[10665,"Option"],[16991,"Option"],[9357,"Optional extras"],[14028,"Optional extras"],[14352,"Optional extras"],[16930,"Optional extras"],[12194,"Optional extras only where a platform limit requires one: `gptsovits-ja` (`pyopenjtalk==0.4.1`, source only), `gptsovits-ko`, `mizuoto-indextts[ja]`"],[12379,"Optional features: install spec → the modules it provides, e.g. GPT-SoVITS's `{\"mizuoto[gptsovits-ja]\": (\"pyopenjtalk\",), \"mizuoto[gptsovits-ko]\": (\"mecab\", \"jamo\")}`; `mizuoto doctor` lists the ones that do not import"],[16146,"Optionally paste a script under **Script** (see the next section) and choose **Make a line of each**: **line of text** or **sentence**."],[10309,"Options"],[10318,"Options"],[10327,"Options"],[10353,"Options"],[10362,"Options"],[10371,"Options"],[10386,"Options"],[10411,"Options"],[10439,"Options"],[10448,"Options"],[10470,"Options"],[10587,"Options"],[10602,"Options"],[10634,"Options"],[10649,"Options"],[16065,"Options"],[16105,"Options"],[16395,"Or **Each model's own repository**. **mizuoto-model mirrors the files Mizuoto downloads; what it lacks comes from each model's own repository.** The mirror is fetched from the chosen download source too"],[16353,"Or 16–48 kHz"],[10221,"Or a clip of the target voice"],[9713,"or click **Accept the licence** in **Models** › **Engines** and tick **I have read and accept this licence**. The acceptance is stored as `engines.<id>.accepted_licence` (the licence's id and version); a new licence version must be accepted again."],[8933,"Or click **Accept the licence** in the web UI's **Models** › **Engines**."],[16378,"Or the CPU or one GPU. **A fine-tune takes the device for itself while it runs**"],[9107,"Or the whole catalogue, downloaded for it: `python scripts/mirror_fetch.py /srv/mirror/team/mizuoto-model/resolve/main`."],[8940,"Order and fallback"],[9190,"Other calls:"],[11011,"Other names for models, for the OpenAI-compatible endpoint: `{\"tts-1\": \"qwen3tts/1.7b-base\"}`"],[10781,"Other origins allowed to send state-changing requests (CORS is enabled for them too)"],[12144,"Other programs learn the actual port: a line `SERVER_READY url=…` on standard output, and `server.json` (host, port, URL, process id) in the data folder, removed on shutdown. `mizuoto runtime` and friends find the running server through it. The front end derives the back end's address from the URL it was loaded from and needs no notice."],[16651,"other warnings, and **Licences of the clips**."],[12524,"Otherwise"],[9010,"Otherwise (or with `--name`) it becomes a user model `<engine>/<name>`; the name cannot be a catalogue model's."],[16094,"otherwise it imports it as a user model, `engine/folder-name`."],[11340,"Otherwise the model's `AccelPolicy` is resolved when it loads (`policy_for(name, strict)`: one per value, so models share resolutions) and reported as `LoadedModelInfo.attention`. `LocalHandle` binds it for each step of a request with `RequestContext.accel` (the context variable lives in `runtime/context.py`, so binding loads no torch), so a stream suspended between steps never leaks its policy to another thread."],[11145,"Output and `--json`"],[71,"outputs"],[8609,"outputs"],[10110,"Outputs and jobs"],[9941,"Outputs, history, jobs and their logs"],[14550,"Over ≥ 20 texts × 3 voices × 3 seeds per voice per voice mode and model: mean CER/WER (Whisper large-v3-turbo) ≤ reference + 0.5 pp, and no case worse than the reference's worst + 5 pp; speaker similarity (CAM++ cosine to the reference clip) mean ≥ reference − 0.01; duration ratio within ±5 %; UTMOS mean ≥ reference − 0.05; loudness and F0 median within the reference's interquartile range, per voice. Failed clips (error rate above 50 %) are compared on their own (Fisher's exact test) and left out of the other measures; a threshold exceeded fails only when the paired difference is significant (Wilcoxon, p \\< 0.05)"],[10747,"Override one setting, e.g. `MIZUOTO_SERVER__PORT=8000` or `MIZUOTO_DOWNLOADS__SOURCE=hf-mirror`"],[11057,"Overrides `compute.attention` for this engine's models"],[11045,"Overrides `compute.unload_after_minutes` for this engine"],[11053,"Overrides `compute.vram_mode` for this engine's models (`auto`: the global one)"],[9785,"overrides the above for one engine"],[10063,"Overview"],[11141,"Overview"],[14041,"Packages"],[14057,"Packages"],[14365,"Packages"],[10870,"Page-locked RAM for the host copies of weights, streamed or kept for a reload (MB; 0: automatic)"],[9824,"page-locked RAM for the host copies of weights, those that stream to a GPU and those kept to reload a model (faster copies; `0`: up to 40 % of RAM on Windows, more on Linux)"],[13818,"Pageable"],[15039,"Pages"],[14186,"Pages are in `site/content/docs/`: `<slug>.mdx` in Simplified Chinese (the default language, `zh-CN`) and `<slug>.en.mdx` in English, with the same structure. The sidebars are `meta.json` and `meta.en.json`, grouped by `---Title---` separators."],[15090,"Paraformer (Chinese)"],[6552,"Paraformer（中文）"],[8824,"Parameter"],[8614,"Parameter presets"],[9173,"Parameter presets"],[11783,"Parameter presets"],[10467,"Parameter presets: a named set of parameters for one model, or common parameters only when no model is named."],[15766,"Parameters"],[16432,"Parameters"],[15007,"Parameters and engine options are a model's own: a new model starts from its defaults or its default preset. \"Run again\" sets them for the new model in the same watcher that resets them."],[8853,"Parameters are lenient here: one the model does not take is dropped rather than refused. Errors take OpenAI's shape, `{\"error\": {\"message\", \"type\", \"param\", \"code\"}}`, with Mizuoto's error code as `code`. A successful answer carries `X-Mizuoto-Job` and `X-Mizuoto-Model` headers."],[12304,"Parameters, options and load options"],[15089,"Parity"],[15160,"Parity"],[15262,"Parity"],[15318,"Parity"],[15326,"Parity"],[15433,"Parity"],[15525,"Parity"],[15624,"Parity"],[15685,"Parity"],[15761,"Parity"],[14430,"Parity with the references"],[12129,"Parsing `/openapi.json` at run time into node templates"],[12319,"Part"],[12478,"Part"],[14207,"Part"],[12706,"Partly loaded models"],[9854,"Partly loaded models run their layers' weights through RAM each time they run: a language model pays it for every generated frame, so the more of it fits, the faster it goes. Copies overlap the computation on NVIDIA and AMD GPUs; on Intel GPUs they are synchronous."],[12583,"partly loaded ones (already slow; ComfyUI's first key);"],[13271,"Partly loaded, 2 side streams"],[12587,"Partly loading a phase's components: the smaller ones load whole first, each leaving the others at least their minimum, and the largest gets what