bus: `subscribe(handler)`"],[11650,"The events today: `settings_changed`, `job_updated`, `job_log`, `jobs_cleared`, `outputs_added`, `outputs_removed`, `runtime_changed`, `compute_changed`, `engines_changed`, `voices_changed`, `datasets_changed`, `projects_changed`, `experiments_changed`, `train_metrics`, `presets_changed`, `models_changed`. Each carries a snapshot, never a live object: the bridge serialises it later on the event loop while job threads keep writing. The bridge subscribes to the EventBus (called from threads, it crosses into the loop with `call_soon_threadsafe`) and emits each event under its name."],[12948,"The exact path is 5 % behind qwen-tts-webui, the fused one level with it, both in 12 % less memory; the exact path's audio repeats sample for sample between rounds."],[16667,"The experiment's page shows the base model, the dataset, the result and the language. **Stages** is a row of steps, each **Not run**, **Running**, **Done**, **Out of date** or **Failed**."],[11085,"The export stage speaks a dataset clip's text with what was trained"],[15255,"The F5-TTS engine as implemented in Mizuoto: v1 Base, v0 Base and E2, the DiT and UNetT, the CFM sampler and Vocos, what reproduces upstream exactly, memory and compile notes, the full fine-tune, and its parity results."],[15253,"The fast decoding path is CUDA only."],[11862,"The file is checked for outside changes every second; every change, wherever it came from, reaches the `on_keys_change` listeners as dotted keys (`changed_keys`)."],[14746,"The first job, `scope`, reads the changed files (a push's from the compare API, a pull request's from its file list) and `python scripts/ci.py scope` maps them to checks:"],[13072,"The first measurement on a free GPU (conditions above), of commit `4e6fe35`, frozen in a worktree. Every engine ran with its GPU defaults (`dtype = auto`, CUDA graphs on), three runs per case in one process per engine, with two streamed cases added. Warm is the faster of the two later runs; the first request includes the model's load."],[14740,"The first opt-in runs exposed a harness bug: requests and the parity cases had put engine options under `options`, which the request model does not have and pydantic ignores, so `packed_guidance` and six T3 cases (GPT-SoVITS's cut5, batch and serial cases, VoxCPM's continuation and retry) had run with the defaults. They now use `engine_options`; rerun on the CPU, the six are identical to 0.1 and upstream sample for sample with their options applied."],[16994,"The first port to try, from the settings by default (7869); `0` picks any free port"],[13954,"The first request pays the compilation: +30 s to +160 s. The audio is not identical (Acceleration)."],[9876,"The first requests pay the compilation: on a CPU, 30 s to 160 s more."],[15986,"The first synthesis"],[16023,"The first synthesis loads the model into the server's process, which takes a while; then the model stays in memory until it has been idle for the time set under **Settings › Compute**. When the GPU has less free memory than the model needs, Mizuoto fails at once with **The GPU is not available or ran out of memory**, and **What to do** says how to fix it, such as another device or freeing GPU memory."],[16440,"The first time, the screen picks **Settings › Speech › Default model**, or else the first model that is ready. Then it remembers your last choice."],[12984,"The first two save about 5 % of the attention (under 1 % of a frame). The third saves about 20 % (about 2 % of a frame at 300 positions, 7 % at 1,200), but it holds four times the keys and values on the device. None was made."],[15311,"The Fish Speech engine as implemented in Mizuoto's separate mizuoto-fishspeech distribution: S2 Pro's dual-AR transformer and the 44.1 kHz codec, Drama 3's mixture-of-experts backbone and codebook tower, what reproduces upstream exactly, one wait per frame and CUDA graphs, experts streamed by the row, the LoRA fine-tune, and parity results."],[9866,"the