ig.json`, `model.safetensors` (else `pytorch_model.bin`), `audiovae.pth` (else `audiovae.safetensors`), `tokenizer.json` and `tokenizer_config.json`. A voice's cache holds the VAE latents of the prompt (left-padded) and of the reference (right-padded), as upstream's `build_prompt_cache` makes them."],[12877,"The generator jumped ahead instead of drawing: MT19937's state after *n* draws computed in GF(2) (`mizuoto/training/rng.py`), 204 jumps in 2.3 s instead of 41–52 s"],[15505,"The GPT is small and launch-bound: a step is about 360 small kernels and used to wait for the device twice (upstream's two end-of-sequence checks), plus a Python boolean copied to the device by top-p. Now the two checks are read together (the same boolean) and the copy is a `fill_`: one wait per step. With `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the GPT wholly on its device) its one-token steps run as graphs around each layer's attention, one set per number of rows (rows drop as they finish); the cache, grown by concatenation, and the sampling stay eager on the request's generator. A voice's own GPT gets its own graphs. The real v2, v2Pro and v4 models give the same audio with and without graphs, 1.3–2.0 times faster per request."],[11513,"the GPT-2's one-token steps around each layer's attention; the cache, its beam reorder and the sampling eager"],[15426,"The GPT-SoVITS engine as implemented in Mizuoto: v2, v2Pro, v2ProPlus, v4 and v5 Turbo, the text front end with its ported converters and models, the T2S model, SoVITS and the flow, what reproduces upstream exactly, GPU decoding, the speaker fine-tune that writes upstream's files, and its parity results."],[12616,"the GPU's own noise"],[11481,"The graphs' own generator is registered with each capture (`register_generator_state`) only before torch 2.14. From 2.14 a capture registers every generator it draws from by itself, and the call is a deprecated no-op that warned at each capture."],[10002,"The handshake succeeded"],[12439,"The HiggsAudio v2 tokenizer: `nn/codecs/dac`, `nn/ssl/hubert`, residual codebooks"],[16025,"The History screen: every result, to search, filter by model, mark as favourite, run again, download and delete."],[14338,"The host connects and sends `hello` with the token (compared with `hmac.compare_digest`) and its protocol. An agent of another protocol refuses the host with a hint to install the same Mizuoto version on both machines, and the host refuses such an agent in turn. Otherwise the agent answers with its `AgentInfo`: version, devices, which engines are available there and its installed models."],[9265,"The host enters the child app's `lifespan` on its own event loop (it forwards events to the socket) and calls `services.close()` on the way out. `start_background=True` starts the job scheduler and the unloading of idle models; without it, queued jobs do not run. `create_app` also takes `extra_hosts` (a set; names added to it later are accepted at once) and `serve_ui=False` (the API only)."],[9996,"The host is contacted at once: online, the command prints the agent's machine name, Mizuoto version, devices and installed engines; unreachable, the host is saved anyway and its state (`offline` or `refused`) is shown."],[12671,"The host optimizer keeps the float32 copies and the gradients in one buffer each and moves a step's gradients and parameters through one page-locked buffer per device dtype, with one wait; most of its step is AdamW's own arithmetic on the CPU (Qwen3-TTS 1.7B: about 4.5 s of its 5.5 s step), which only a fused optimizer, with other results, would shorten. A `lowest` stage runs without torch's huge pages (`compute.cpu_allocator`): with them its per-step allocations stalled in the kernel's compaction and the run took 2.2× as long."],[14342,"The host plans against its own catalogue and the agent's model list; the agent handles its own GPU memory, and training always stays local."],[12252,"The host probes devices without importing torch: nvidia-smi, rocm-smi / amd-smi