yUI is a source of patterns, not a code base adopted: Mizuoto keeps its own services, jobs, API, command line and UI, and code comments name the ComfyUI counterpart of each piece."],[16347,"The model Speak chooses the first time, and the one the OpenAI-compatible endpoint uses when the request names no model it knows"],[12229,"The model takes a closed attribute vocabulary"],[10460,"The model to load, e.g. `gptsovits/v2pro-base`"],[10967,"The model used when none is named (command line, OpenAI-compatible endpoint)"],[12160,"The model wrapper (`ModelPatcher`)"],[14299,"The model's attention policy, bound with the context (Acceleration)"],[9904,"the model's variant takes **Batches** of at least 2: Qwen3-TTS (8), GPT-SoVITS (20), OmniVoice (8);"],[9038,"The models folder; default: the data folder's"],[11635,"The models live in the server's process, so the API is how other programs (and `mizuoto runtime`) see and free them. `routers/runtime.py`:"],[10373,"The models Mizuoto knows, and their states"],[15998,"The models of Fish Speech and IndexTTS cannot be downloaded until their licences are accepted. See Licence-gated engines below."],[16060,"The Models screen: download, verify, delete and import catalogue models; engine cards (availability, device, precision, enabled, options, checks, licence); and shared files."],[17038,"The models, voices, results and cache folders can be moved under **Settings › Storage** (for example `models/` to a larger disk)."],[9083,"The ModelScope repository"],[11003,"The most characters in one request (at least 100)"],[16161,"the name is already in the cast;"],[11768,"The native runtime (built lazily), which engines are implemented here, their extras and trainers"],[14093,"The native trainers"],[16798,"The navigation is on the left. In a narrow window (a phone) it moves to the bottom, which shows the first four screens and **More**; More opens the rest (**Train**, **Models**, **History**, **Settings**):"],[15636,"The network: the bidirectional Qwen3 over text and audio codes (`audio_embeddings`, `audio_heads`)"],[16193,"The new line keeps this line's speaker"],[9256,"The object is also a context manager:"],[8959,"The official repositories"],[13752,"The old rule of thumb was under nearly all of them (GPT-SoVITS 5×, VoxCPM's `lowest` LoRA up to 3.4×), and said 14.1 GB for Fish Speech's LoRA, which runs out of a 24 GB card at its default batch. Estimates are now these peaks scaled by the base model's size, plus a tenth and 512 MB, and follow the batch where the peak does; the warning names a batch that fits when no preset does."],[15617,"The OmniVoice engine as implemented in Mizuoto: the bidirectional Qwen3 with iterative unmasking, the HiggsAudio v2 tokenizer (DAC and HuBERT), pydub's arithmetic without pydub, what reproduces upstream exactly, the full and LoRA fine-tunes, and its parity results."],[11504,"the one-token steps (`DecoderSteps`) and the draw, a graph per EOS mask; upstream's nucleus loop replayed on the device (`nucleus_device`)"],[8574,"The OpenAPI schema also lists the socket's event types, so a client's types can be generated from it."],[12294,"The OpenAPI schema is generated without `separate_input_output_schemas=False`"],[12670,"the optimizer's sums may differ in the last bits on a GPU"],[12198,"The optional attention packages (flash-attn, xFormers, SageAttention) are backends only, with version checks, self-tests and fallbacks, never dependencies"],[15744,"The order comes from a plain shuffled data loader on the process-wide generator (the training stage's own process). Accelerate's gradient accumulation is reproduced as the loss over the steps, an optimiser step every N batches and at each epoch's end."],[14996,"The other `*_changed` events invalidate their keys through `createInvalidator()`, so a burst within 300 ms causes one refetch."],[16790,"The other commands (`add-ref`, `set-transcript`, `retranscribe`, `edit`, `remove`…) are in `mizuoto voice --help` and the command reference.