scripts read line by line by a cast of voices) is the most recent complete screen and makes a good template. Its API is `mizuoto/api/routers/projects.py`; its event is `projects_changed`."],[16122,"The Projects screen: a cast of voices reads a book, a script or a dialogue line by line; importing scripts, editing lines, rendering, takes and exporting audio with subtitles."],[15389,"The prompt (a chat: system turn with `[Reference i]` blocks, earlier chunks as finished turns, the open voice turn), text checks, long-text chunks and their history"],[15709,"The prompt as `Qwen3TTSForConditionalGeneration.generate` builds it, the talker loop, chunked decoding, voice caches"],[15330,"The prompt is a ChatML conversation: a system turn holding each reference's text and its codes, then the text to speak. The **slow transformer** (Qwen3-4B-shaped: 36 layers, q/k RMSNorm, one fused `wqkv`) generates a frame's semantic token; the **fast transformer** (4 layers) generates the other nine codebooks from the slow model's normed hidden state. The **codec** (a modified DAC at 44.1 kHz: causal convolutions, a windowed transformer, a downsampling residual quantiser with one semantic codebook of 4096 and nine of 1024; about 21.5 frames a second) encodes references and decodes frames into audio. Text is generated in batches of speaker turns, each batch decoded as it finishes."],[11854,"The protocol version is `AGENT_PROTOCOL = 2`. At `hello` the token is compared with `hmac.compare_digest` and the protocol checked; a host and an agent of different protocols refuse each other with an upgrade hint."],[14347,"The Python environment"],[8901,"The Python of the image (`python:<version>-slim`)"],[15943,"The Qwen2/Qwen3 decoder with transformers' numerics (`hf_sdpa`, `mask_for`), `DynamicCache` and the optional preallocated `BufferCache`"],[15677,"The Qwen3-TTS engine as implemented in Mizuoto: variants and files, the talker, code predictor, speaker encoder and 12 Hz codec, what reproduces upstream exactly, memory and CUDA-graph decoding, the speaker fine-tune, and its parity results."],[15142,"The randomness: upstream draws the dither from torch's global generator, and its layer stacks (`MultiSequential`) draw one uniform number per layer at every forward for a layer drop that does nothing at inference. Both move the generator the next segment's dither draws from; the port draws both from one generator in the same order."],[13002,"The real CosyVoice 2 LM (2 GB, it fit), 150 tokens, ms per token:"],[13057,"The real models did not fit wholly beside the other workload, so through the stack their weights streamed and graphs did not engage: the removed waits alone gave v1.5 10.25 → 9.59 s and v2 36.3 → 33.4 s (×1.07–1.09), identical audio. The decoding loop at the 1.5 GPT's sizes, 4 or 8 of its 24 layers, random weights, fp16, three beams, 120 steps; ms per step:"],[10991,"The recogniser for clips whose language is Chinese, used once it is downloaded (`asr/paraformer-zh`: Paraformer with punctuation, as GPT-SoVITS transcribes Chinese); empty: `tts.asr_model` for every language"],[10215,"The recording to convert"],[10232,"The recording to edit"],[10236,"The recording's whole text after the edit (required)"],[15843,"The reference"],[11426,"The reference ignores it and uses the dense mask, so `auto` is unchanged. Qwen's `mask_for` returns `Masked(dense, info)`; VoxCPM's steps, Seed-VC, GPT-SoVITS v4/v5 and Fish Speech's codec give theirs. With `dispatch.DEBUG` on (the tiny engines' tests), every call checks that `mask_info` describes its dense mask; `MIZUOTO_TEST_ACCEL=count` checks that every site of every tiny engine and trainer goes through the dispatcher."],[15244,"The reference is upstream on torch 2.8 (on its own torch 2.3.1 it disagrees with itself on 2.8). With upstream's voice prompt fed to both, cloning (English, Chinese with numbers), cross-lingual cloning, instructions, preset speakers, streamed audio and voice conversion are identical sample for sample for v1, v2 and v3. Through the stack, each side making its own prompt:"],[14494,"The reference to clone comes from `MIZUOTO_TEST_REFERENCE` (plus `MIZUOTO_TEST_REFERENCE_TEXT`), else an installed preset or design model speaks one. Licence-gated engines take part only with `MIZUOTO_TEST_ACCEPT_LICENCES=1` (and their packages installed), and their licences are accepted in the temporary folder only."],[11882,"The registered kinds are `speak`, `voice_prepare`, `convert`, `edit`, `engine_op`, `transcribe`, `model_download`, `asset_download`, `dataset_prepare`, `train`, `project_render` and `project_export`."],[11432,"The registry, policies, fallbacks, strict mode and binding are tested on the CPU, with real models through every site (identical audio, metrics and weights with `auto`) and the optional backends' glue against fake packages computing the same maths. On NVIDIA (RTX 3090, torch 2.8, flash-attn 2.8.3, xFormers 0.0.32.post2, SageAttention 1.0.6) every backend was checked on every site's recorded calls, through every engine and every trainer: the results and what they decided. SageAttention 3 (Blackwell) is not checked."],[10636,"The remote hosts: address, state, version, devices, engines, the engines using it"],[16552,"The report"],[9090,"The repository to check"],[14197,"The request context"],[14285,"The request's `random.Random`, seeded the same way"],[14283,"The request's `torch.Generator` on a device, one per device, seeded with the request's seed (fresh entropy without one)"],[12592,"the request's generators, its `rng` and any the engine names (`generators=`) are put back as they were before the first attempt;"],[12407,"The requests and results are standard-library dataclasses in `mizuoto/core/inference/tasks.py`, re-exported by `mizuoto.runtime.engine`:"],[16873,"The REST API, a WebSocket for events and streamed audio, an OpenAI-compatible `/v1/audio/speech`, and Python."],[14523,"The result: on the CPU in fp32, every engine is identical to its reference (VoxCPM in bf16 too), except CosyVoice when each side makes its own voice prompt: CAM++'s speaker embedding differs from onnxruntime's by about 1e-6, and HiFT's sine source accumulates and amplifies that along the utterance; given the same voice prompt, CosyVoice is identical sample for sample too. Every trainer gives upstream's losses, learning rates and weights byte for byte on the CPU when both are seeded alike."],[12191,"The right build depends on the hardware and driver, which no package manager can choose for the user"],[13268,"The rotary tables, IndexTTS's in-place GELU and Fish Speech's Snake give their reference's bits on CUDA in fp32, fp16 and bf16 (the exactness tests now run on CUDA when a GPU is visible); CosyVoice's U-Net mask is the same tensor made once. Fish Speech's GPU training replays upstream's initialisation on the CPU generator, as upstream builds its model on the CPU."],[15642,"The rule-based duration estimate, upstream's tables"],[12267,"The run holds the device once; the UI and the fingerprints know the stages without running anything"],[10567,"The run's memory plan before it starts: the device it takes, roughly what it holds there under each `training.memory` setting against the free memory now, and the setting or smaller batch that would fit"],[10037,"The running request fails; the next one reconnects"],[9909,"The running request takes the queued requests of its group just before calling the engine; when the batch fails, they go back to the queue and run one by one. The command line runs one job at a time in the foreground, so only the server (web UI, HTTP API) batches."],[14193,"The runtime"],[12422,"The runtime finds an implementation by id (`get_engine` in `mizuoto/runtime/engine.py`):"],[11544,"The runtime routes"],[12327,"The runtime, in the server's process"],[11454,"the s2mel DiT and BigVGAN (also turned on by its load option `use_torch_compile`)"],[9870,"the s2mel DiT and BigVGAN (also turned on by the load option `use_torch_compile`)"],[13730,"the same"],[13895,"the same"],[13900,"the same"],[13905,"the same"],[13910,"the same"],[13915,"the same"],[13920,"the same"],[13925,"the same"],[13930,"the same"],[8543,"The same as the command line"],[13071,"The same changes help the CPU a little: Qwen3-TTS `cv-en-aiden` 17.05 → 16.76 s, `base-clone-en` 26.19 → 25.83 s, audio identical."],[9701,"The same check shows in **Settings** › **Compute**. \"sees no GPU: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES hides them\" means the variable is set where Mizuoto starts."],[15740,"The same codes as eager; on the decode loop of the 1.7B sizes 2.7–3.4 times faster than the loop with its waits."],[9845,"The same for CosyVoice 2 and 3's language model: about 1 % faster on a GPU, 2–5 % with `fp16`; may be no longer bit-identical there"],[9809,"the same for one engine's models (`auto`: the global setting). UI: **GPU memory for this engine** on its card"],[17051,"The same from the command line"],[16162,"the same name begins two or more lines;"],[12804,"the same operations in the same order"],[12882,"the same operations in the same order"],[11824,"The same path has a few more entrances, all ending in `TtsService`'s one planning and one job: streamed output (a `StreamSink`: the WebSocket `/api/v1/tts/stream`, `POST /tts/speak?stream=true`, `mizuoto speak --stream`), streamed text input (a `TextFeed`, for variants with `stream_text_input`), voice conversion and speech editing (the `convert` and `edit` jobs), and the OpenAI-compatible `POST /v1/audio/speech` (`TtsService.from_openai` maps the model, voice, `instructions`, `speed` and format onto a `SpeakRequest`). The protocols and examples are in HTTP API."],[14481,"The same seed repeats sample for sample; two sentences that do not fit one segment become two segments (or the engine handles long text itself)"],[12802,"the same tensor"],[12800,"the same values"],[12880,"the same values"],[14221,"The same, for a device named `<host>/<device>`: a session with `mizuoto agent` on another machine"],[11331,"the same, or `inherit`"],[15794,"The scalar quantiser, the local encoder, the local DiT (v1 and v2), the CFM's Euler sampler, the prompt sequence, `PatchDecoder` and the generation loop"],[12075,"The scope is the part affected: `runtime`, `webui`, `training`, `models`, `scripts`, `site`, or an engine id (`qwen3tts`, `gptsovits`…); several may be listed (`runtime,training`), or none for a change across the board."],[16796,"The screens"],[16125,"The script format"],[16163,"the script is a dialogue (some name meets one of the two rules above) and the prefix **looks like a name**: it starts with a letter and has at most three words, such as `Dr. Watson` or `林黛玉`."],[9978,"The second line lists the engines available there. Later starts reuse the saved token; to see it again, open that machine's `settings.toml` (`mizuoto config path`)."],[11803,"The server (`mizuoto webui`)"],[8558,"The server `mizuoto webui` starts serves the web UI and an HTTP API. The web UI does everything through this API, so scripts and other programs can do the same things."],[8816,"The server answers `{\"type\": \"queued\", \"job_id\": …}`."],[12140,"The server decides whether a port is free by **binding** it, not by connecting to it (`bind_first_free_port` in `mizuoto/core/net/ports.py`):"],[12136,"The server finds `dist/` through the package's `__path__` (`web_dist_dir()` in `api/static.py`): one line for a source checkout, an installed wheel and a container. `SPAStaticFiles` is mounted last, so it only receives paths the API, the socket and the docs did not match. Without a build it logs a warning and serves the API only, which is the normal state while working on the back end."],[8927,"The server in the container binds `0.0.0.0`, where Mizuoto no longer checks the `Host` header: anyone who reaches the port can do everything (download models, delete files). Set a token with `MIZUOTO_SERVER__ACCESS_TOKEN`, or publish the port on this machine only: `-p 127.0.0.1:7869:7869`."],[8789,"The server pushes events over socket.io at `/ws` (socket.io path `/ws/socket.io`). Traffic is server to client only: every operation goes through REST, REST is the truth, and events only tell you when to refresh."],[14140,"the server: `/api/v1/app/health`, the UI, and a dummy speak through the API."],[9733,"The server's log"],[9117,"The services"],[9255,"The services the server uses (see above), callable once started"],[9898,"The setting applies to models loaded after the change."],[17021,"The settings file (`mizuoto config path` prints its path)"],[9141,"The settings file itself; wins over `config_dir`"],[9212,"The settings file's full path; wins over `config_dir`"],[15247,"the SFT Chinese case and the v2 Chinese clone differ in length, from normalisation; with normalisation off on both sides the first is identical and the second differs only by CAM++'s noise;"],[10413,"The shared assets and the models that need them"],[11519,"The shared Qwen decoder, without autograd, norms and rotates q and k together on the CPU (on a GPU apart, as transformers does, unless the projections are fused: CUDA sizes a reduction by its tensor, so the joined norm differed in the last bit now and then) and uses `F.rms_norm` where a self-test on the device shows the same bits as the float32-upcast norm (`_fused_norm_exact`: one kernel instead of eight on CUDA in bf16/fp16 with recent torch). `mask_for(padded=…)` skips its device check when the caller knows there is no padding."],[11418,"the site refuses quantised attention (`approx_ok=False`: every autoregressive model's, the Qwen decoder's, IndexTTS's GPT, VoxCPM's MiniCPM, GPT-SoVITS's T2S, Fish Speech's three, Whisper's) and the backend is approximate (SageAttention 2 and 3);"],[12110,"The skeleton is GPL-3.0, and so is Mizuoto (`GPL-3.0-only`). The two licence-gated engines ship apart because of their licences (see the decisions below)."],[12097,"The skeleton itself: all logic in `core` with two thin entrances over it (FastAPI and Typer