nt"],[11469,"the step's embeddings and heads;"],[11510,"the T2S's one-token steps around each layer's attention, a set per number of rows; sampling eager"],[16565,"The tabs at the top switch between **Experiments** and **Datasets**; at the right is **New experiment** or **New dataset**."],[16031,"The takes of a project's lines are **not** listed here; they are managed on the project's page (see Projects). Files **exported** from a project or a chapter are listed."],[15715,"The talker and the code predictor, on `runtime/lm/qwen.py`"],[15734,"The talker's working memory is estimated from the request: each row's prompt (instruction, reference text and codes, text) and 16 frames per text token (speech runs at 3–4), within `max_new_tokens`, the cache's peak counted as one layer above its size, plus 256 MB. A sentence therefore sets aside some 300–400 MB on the 1.7B model, not the gigabytes a worst case (8192 frames) would claim, so the talker is not streamed needlessly when memory is short. `compute.kv_cache = static` gives the talker and the code predictor preallocated caches (identical on the CPU)."],[10219,"The target voice (a library voice)"],[11829,"The task types engines take and give (`SynthesisTask`, `VoiceSpec`, `LoadSpec`, `AudioChunk`, `Description`, `OptionSpec`…), standard-library dataclasses re-exported by `runtime.engine`; the core builds them at module level without loading the runtime"],[14778,"The tests in scope against the oldest torch Mizuoto supports and the newest, to catch torch's API drift"],[15279,"The text (reference transcript plus the new text, Chinese characters turned into pinyin with tones) is embedded by ConvNeXtV2 blocks; the transformer predicts the flow from noise to mel frames, conditioned on the reference's mel; an ODE solver integrates it over a fixed time grid, with classifier-free guidance as a batch of two; Vocos turns the mel into 24 kHz audio. There is no duration model: the length comes from the reference's speaking rate, or from `duration`."],[15477,"The text-to-semantic model: batched and row-by-row decoding, upstream's sampler"],[10136,"The text; `-` reads it from standard input"],[8767,"The text; `texts` is a batch, one result per text (models that take batches)"],[15215,"The three flows; CosyVoice 3's DiT estimator"],[15213,"The three language models, repetition-aware sampling (RAS), the streamed-text interleave (5 text : 15 speech)"],[15012,"The token (localStorage and the `mizuoto_token` cookie), whether one is needed"],[10627,"The token hosts must give (default from settings; made and saved when there is none)"],[11127,"The token hosts must give; `mizuoto agent` makes one when there is none"],[9967,"The token hosts must give; made and saved when there is none"],[14925,"The token layer: `src/theme/`"],[15798,"The tokenizer as transformers 5.3 builds it, upstream's split of multi-character Han tokens, the text normaliser"],[16521,"The Tools screen: say a recording in another voice with CosyVoice, and replace words in a recording with F5-TTS."],[16794,"The top bar"],[16771,"The top shows the name and kind; a designed voice also shows **Designed with** *model* and its description, a preset voice **Speaker** *name* **of** *model*."],[16963,"The torch build: another CUDA (`cu126`…`cu132`), ROCm (`rocm6.4`…`rocm7.2`) or `cpu` index"],[17055,"The torch builds for AMD, Intel, Apple silicon and the CPU, installing from source and Docker are in Installation."],[8895,"The torch requirement, such as `torch==2.8.0`"],[16966,"The torch requirement, such as `torch==2.8.0`"],[11501,"the tower around its 13 layers' attention, then the backbone around its 10 softmax attention layers (`Stretches`); the tower's again per sampling settings; not when the experts stream"],[14802,"The train job"],[16546,"The Train screen: build and prepare datasets, then run each engine's own fine-tuning recipe stage by stage in experiments, with losses and previews, exported as a voice's weights or a new model."],[14829,