 own build on Apple silicon. `mizuoto doctor` compares them and prints the command that installs the right build into Mizuoto's Python, such as:"],[9851,"torch's CUDA allocator: `native`, `async` (cudaMallocAsync; CUDA graphs are not used under it, so decoding is slower), `expandable` (expandable segments: the same results, less memory reserved); applies at the next start"],[10894,"torch's CUDA allocator: `native`, `async` (no CUDA graphs under it), `expandable` (`auto`: native); at the next start"],[5512,"torch（≥ 2.8）、safetensors、soxr、tokenizers"],[822,"torch（2.8 或更新）"],[14080,"torchaudio, librosa, numba, resampy, scipy"],[5542,"torchaudio、librosa、numba、resampy、scipy"],[80,"train"],[8618,"train"],[16545,"Train"],[16860,"Train"],[16862,"Train"],[14804,"Trainer and StageContext"],[6266,"Trainer 与 StageContext"],[14797,"Trainers"],[12208,"Trainers reproduce upstream's recipes, including their training/inference mismatches (Qwen3-TTS's training skips `text_projection`; Fish Speech's training does not scale the codebook embeddings by 1/√11)"],[9288,"Training"],[11155,"Training"],[12473,"Training"],[15159,"Training"],[15261,"Training"],[15317,"Training"],[15432,"Training"],[15524,"Training"],[15623,"Training"],[15684,"Training"],[15760,"Training"],[15857,"Training"],[16297,"Training"],[16878,"Training"],[9945,"Training (always here)"],[16599,"Training always runs on this machine, never on a remote host; when an engine's device is on a remote host, its methods are not available. A fine-tune takes its device for itself while it runs. Choose the device under **Settings › Training › Training device**; by default it is **The engine’s device**."],[8617,"Training datasets"],[10814,"Training experiments"],[9897,"Training has its own setting, `training.attention` (**Settings** › **Training** › **Attention**). It offers only backends with a backward pass, so not SageAttention."],[14799,"Training methods in the manifest"],[16598,"Training needs nothing beyond Mizuoto and torch: every method runs in Mizuoto's own Python, each stage in a process of its own. Some methods need shared files used only for training, such as GPT-SoVITS's pretrained discriminators (`mizuoto asset download gptsovits/s2d-v2pro`). When something is missing, the new-experiment dialog marks the method **not available** and gives the command to run."],[11069,"Training precision: `auto`, `fp32`, `fp16`, `bf16`"],[14306,"Training stages are the one exception: they run in their own process and seed the process-wide generators there (see Trainers)."],[12658,"Training stages run in their own process and own their device: before a GPU stage the host moves every idle model off that GPU, and the train job holds every slot of `gpu:<dev>` (`JobSpec.exclusive`). Inside the stage, `training.memory` chooses a preset of `mizuoto/training/memory.py`'s tools; a method's own hyperparameters win:"],[14867,"Training starts from a dataset. A dataset is `datasets/<slug>/`: `dataset.json`, `manifest.jsonl` (one row per clip: `id`, `audio`, `text`, `speaker`, `language`, `duration`, the rate, `excluded`, the source and `licence_tags`) and `audio/<id>.flac` (at most 48 kHz). The dataset's fingerprint is the SHA-256 of `manifest.jsonl`."],[12508,"Training tools"],[14824,"Training-only shared assets per variant (GPT-SoVITS's pretrained discriminators); `\"*\"` for every variant"],[12848,"Training, one fine-tune per trainer (s), metrics and weight tensors identical (the stages get the CPU settings through their environment):"],[14909,"Training's memory presets (`training.memory`: `standard`, `low`, `lowest`) and tools are in `mizuoto/training/memory.py`: gradient checkpointing puts back the global generators and the trainer's own during the backward recomputation, so losses and weights do not change; `low` adds only tools that keep results, `lowest` also those that change them slightly; a method's own hyperparameters win. A stage on a GPU adds `memory/peak_mb` to its metrics, and `MethodInfo.memory_mb` estimates a run's peak per preset. Details in Memory management."],[14507,"Trains on the workspace's dataset with one implementation and keeps the experiment, metrics, previews and exports"],[10245,"Transcribe a clip with the speech recognition engine."],[10983,"Transcribe a reference clip without a transcript (needs the speech recognition model `tts.asr_model` downloaded)"],[10338,"Transcribe the clips (or this one) again with speech recognition"],[11154,"Transcribe, convert and edit"],[16429,"Transcripts and speech recognition"],[9660,"Transcripts are cached by the audio's SHA-256, the model and the beam width, so the same clip is never transcribed twice with the same settings. `tts.auto_transcribe` (on by default), `tts.asr_model` and `tts.asr_beams` (5 by default) control automatic transcription; see Configuration."],[9350,"transcripts for reference clips and datasets"],[11786,"Transcripts through the `asr` engine, cached by audio SHA-256 and model"],[4561,"transformer 0.90"],[13099,"transformer 0.90"],[4211,"transformer 69.7"],[12749,"transformer 69.7"],[14074,"transformers (several incompatible versions), accelerate, huggingface_hub, peft, loralib"],[15946,"transformers' logits processors in their order; `multinomial`'s own computation without its device waits"],[5536,"transformers（多个互不兼容的版本）、accelerate、huggingface_hub、peft、loralib"],[14020,"Truncating VoxCPM's attention to exactly the filled positions: identical in bf16, not in fp32 (the kernel's blocks change); the cut at a multiple of 256 is identical in both."],[16737,"Try it"],[68,"tts"],[8606,"tts"],[16231,"Two buttons at the bottom of the page:"],[15905,"Two engines have another reference:"],[16920,"Two helper engines are built in as well: **speech recognition** (Whisper large-v3-turbo, which fills in the transcripts of reference clips) and the **dummy engine** (`dummy/default`, nothing to download; it speaks in tones so you can learn the UI first)."],[15662,"Two phases: the audio tokenizer (the voice prompt, then decoding) and the language model. If decoding runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, the tokenizer decodes in tiles of 128 frames (about 5 s), each with the 12 frames its DAC decoder's samples depend on each side: the whole's samples up to the sums' rounding (64 dB SNR on a GPU, where the GPU against the CPU is 63 dB), in 108 MB instead of 1 GB for 60 s. The language model reruns over the whole sequence each step, so it is a `oneshot` model for weight streaming (its largest units stay on the device). Training: gradient checkpointing over the model's layers is identical, LoRA dropout included; `lowest` keeps AdamW's state in RAM (identical on the CPU)."],[15299,"Two phases: the transformer with the mel (every ODE step; guidance doubles the batch) and Vocos. If Vocos runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, it decodes in tiles of 256 frames, each with the 29 frames its samples depend on each side (its kernels and the inverse STFT's window): the whole's samples up to the sums' rounding (`applied.fallbacks` says so)."],[9911,"Two settings make CPU work faster without changing any result (Linux; on other systems they change nothing):"],[15328,"Two variants. `s2_pro` (catalogue model `fishspeech/s2-pro`, this page up to Drama 3): cloning from one to four clips, each with its transcript; inline tags; dialogue between speakers (`<|speaker:i|>`). The model folder holds `config.json`, the weights (`model.safetensors.index.json` and its shards, `model.safetensors`, or `model.pth`), `codec.pth` and the BPE tokenizer files. A voice's cache is `codes.pt`, each reference's codes."],[14377,"ty does not follow an editable install's path hook, so `pyproject.toml` sets `tool.ty.environment.extra-paths` to `packages/native/fishspeech` and `packages/native/indextts`, which resolves `mizuoto_fishspeech` and `mizuoto_indextts` from source. torch and the optional extras' packages are listed in `tool.ty.analysis.allowed-unresolved-imports`."],[14390,"ty 