,"When a job started on another screen finishes or fails, a message pops up at the bottom of the window; a failure's message has an **Open log** button."],[16494,"When a model is picked, its default preset is applied; the chosen voice's own default preset comes first."],[16009,"When a source lacks a file or serves it wrong, the next source is tried (the one in the settings first, then Hugging Face, hf-mirror and ModelScope)."],[16230,"When a speaker's model, voice, language, way of speaking or parameters change, every rendered line of that speaker becomes **Changed since its take**. **Level each take** under Export is a rendering setting too: changing it makes every line stale."],[9859,"When a step of a request runs out of memory anyway (an estimate was short, another program took memory), Mizuoto moves the other idle models off that GPU, leaves half of the step's own weights in RAM and runs the step again with the same random draws, so the result is the same, only slower; it tries twice. When that is not enough, and `compute.oom_fallback` is on, an engine with a cheaper way uses it (speech recognition one 30 s window at a time, GPT-SoVITS one text at a time, F5-TTS's, Fish Speech's, IndexTTS's, OmniVoice's and VoxCPM's decoders in tiles). Otherwise the request fails with `compute_unavailable` (`detail.reason` is `out_of_memory`), and, as ComfyUI does, Mizuoto unloads every model not in use from every GPU, so the next try starts on empty devices (models on the CPU stay). If it fails again, give the engine another device, set `compute.vram_mode` to `low` or `none`, or lower `compute.max_resident_models`. Mizuoto also remembers how much memory each step really used and sets that much aside the next time."],[9830,"when a step runs out of GPU memory, run it again with more of its weights in RAM: the same result, slower"],[12246,"When a training run's estimated memory exceeds the free memory, the log warns with the preset that would fit; the run is not refused"],[16452,"When all is done the **Speak** button is back."],[9737,"When an engine fails, the request fails with `engine_error` (exit code 10), whose detail carries the exception and its traceback (**Details** under the error in the web UI; the job's `error` in `mizuoto job show <job id> --json`). The **Models in memory** panel lists an engine whose last request failed, with the error."],[16103,"When an engine has load options, its card has **Options**:"],[14336,"When an engine's device is `<host>/<device>` (for example `engines.qwen3tts.device = \"gpu-box/cuda:0\"`), `RuntimeService.engine` asks `RemoteService` for a `RemoteEngine`: a session with the `mizuoto agent` on that host for one engine on one device. The agent is a whole Mizuoto with its own data folder, models and runtime; it runs the engine in its own process exactly as a host does. `RemoteEngineHandle` answers the same calls as `LocalHandle`. For the user-facing set-up, see Remote engines."],[9725,"When every source fails the job ends with `download_failed` (exit code 12), whose detail lists the sources tried and the last errors."],[12582,"When free memory falls short, idle components on the same device give up the shortfall, in this order:"],[8817,"When generation starts: `{\"type\": \"start\", \"job_id\": …, \"sample_rate\": 24000, \"granularity\": \"token\" | \"segment\" | \"emulated\"}`."],[9709,"When memory runs out during a request anyway, Mizuoto runs the step again with more of its weights in RAM and the same random draws (the same result, slower); with `compute.oom_fallback` it then tries a cheaper way (tiles, smaller batches). `compute.gpu_jobs` (default 1) sets how many jobs run at once on one GPU; a job waiting for the GPU can be started beside the running one with **Run anyway** when the memory suffices. `compute.inference_jobs` (default 1) sets how many synthesis jobs run at once across all engines and devices. More in Performance."],[9933,"When one machine has the GPU and another is where you use Mizuoto, an engine can run on the GPU machine. That machine runs `mizuoto agent` (the **agent** below); the machine you use (the **host** below) adds it as a remote host and sets the engine's device to `<name>/<device>`, for example `gpu-box/cuda:0`. Synthesis, streaming and cancelling then work as they do locally; only the engine, and the models it loads, run on the agent."],[11017,"When requests are batched: Performance."],[9930,"When something fails"],[9672,"When something goes wrong, read the job's log first (**Log** in the **Jobs** panel, or `mizuoto job log <job id>`), then run `mizuoto doctor`: it checks torch's build against the hardware, whether each engine is available and which optional extras are missing, and gives the commands that fix what it finds."],[16543,"When something is missing the footer says so: **Add the recording**, **Give the text after the edit**, or **Mark what to replace: from and to, in seconds**."],[12068,"When the API changes, regenerate the types and commit them, or `typegen-check` fails. UI changes pass the rule tests (imports, tokens, layout, layers, i18n keys)."],[16825,"When the chosen model is not ready yet, the main button is replaced by the one step it still needs — **Enable**, **Accept the** *engine* **licence**, the command that installs what the engine needs (torch, or a licence-gated engine's package) or **Download** *model* *(size)* — with its progress while it runs."],[17070,"When the download is done the **Speak** button is back. Pick a **Preset speaker**, optionally write an instruction under **Style** › **How to say it** (such as \"Cheerfully, a little faster\"), and click **Speak**."],[16093,"when the file sizes match a catalogue model, it checks their SHA-256 and imports the folder as that model;"],[9009,"When the file sizes match a catalogue model's manifest exactly, the folder becomes that catalogue model and every file's SHA-256 is then checked; a mismatch is an error."],[9264,"When the host program is itself a FastAPI (or other ASGI) application, it can mount Mizuoto instead of opening another port:"],[16425,"When the model is not ready"],[16663,"When the result is a voice's weights, **Voice to give the weights**: a library voice, or **A new voice** (made from three of the dataset's clips of 3 to 10 seconds)."],[17056,"When the server is ready the terminal prints `SERVER_READY url=http://127.0.0.1:7869`, and a browser opens that address a moment later. The default port is **7869**, and only this machine can connect by default. Press Ctrl+C to stop the server."],[16091,"When you already have a model's files (an earlier download, a copy from elsewhere, a fine-tune), click **Import a model folder** and choose a folder on the server. The button shows only in a browser on the server machine."],[16728,"When you pick a method for a new experiment, the dialog shows roughly how much GPU memory a run needs with each Memory setting; the experiment's page shows, in **GPU memory**, the free memory of the GPU it would train on and each setting's estimate, marks the ones that do not fit, and when the current one does not, offers the change that would fit with one button (**Use Lowest**, or **Set Batch size to 3** where no setting helps); a run whose estimate exceeds the GPU's free memory also says so in its log, with the setting that would fit, or a smaller `batch_size` where no setting helps (Fish Speech's LoRA at its default batch of 4 needs more than a 24 GB card under *Standard*; under *Lowest* it fits one). On a GPU each logged step also reports **memory/peak_mb**, what it really used."],[12320,"Where"],[14527,"Where"],[15047,"Where"],[15989,"Where"],[12977,"Where a graphed frame's 64 ms go (`--torch-profile`, clone-en, 95 frames; the device busy 97 % of the time):"],[16195,"Where a paragraph ends, for the pauses when exported"],[8823,"Where a WebSocket is awkward, add `stream=true` to the same request: the response is the audio as it is made (chunked transfer):"],[10396,"Where files come from: Model downloads and mirrors."],[16745,"Where it comes from"],[12461,"Where it lives"],[9119,"Where jobs run"],[12796,"where memory comes from and where threads run, not what is computed; the same thread count splits the work the same way"],[12119,"Where Mizuoto differs on purpose:"],[12078,"Where Mizuoto's design comes from: the skeleton's lineage, what was taken from InvokeAI, ani2xcur, Material Design 3 and ComfyUI and what was not, and a table of design decisions with their reasons."],[8938,"Where model files come from, how Mizuoto falls back between sources, resumes and verifies them, and how to use the mizuoto-model mirror or run your own."],[10939,"Where model files come from: `huggingface`, `hf-mirror`, `modelscope` or `custom`; a file a source lacks comes from the next"],[9743,"Where models run and how long they stay loaded, GPU memory (models larger than the GPU, running out of memory), precision, attention backends, torch.compile, and running waiting requests together."],[10698,"Where settings come from"],[16933,"Where the data lives"],[11033,"Where the engine runs: `auto`, `cpu`, `cuda:1`…; `<host>/<device>` (such as `gpu-box/cuda:0`) runs it on a remote host"],[9760,"where the engine runs: `auto`, `cpu`, `cuda:N` (NVIDIA, or AMD under ROCm), `xpu:N` (Intel), `mps` (Apple silicon); `<host>/<device>` runs it on a remote host (see Remote hosts). UI: **Device** on the engine's card"],[16028,"Where the files are"],[12683,"Where the time goes on the CPU"],[8892,"Where torch comes from, hence its build: another CUDA (`cu126` … `cu132`), ROCm (`rocm6.4` … `rocm7.2`) or `cpu` index of download.pytorch.org"],[14160,"Where torch comes from: a CUDA (`cu126` … `cu132`), ROCm (`rocm6.4` … `rocm7.2`) or `cpu` index"],[15981,"Where you start"],[15980,"Where you start, checking torch and the engines, downloading models, licence-gated engines, and the first real synthesis."],[16309,"Whether `mizuoto webui` opens a browser"],[11025,"Whether the engine is enabled"],[9745,"Which GPUs Mizuoto finds"],[16736,"Which models can use it"],[12486,"Which parts of a module may stay off the device and which are fixed"],[14163,"Which torch"],[14938,"While developing, `python scripts/dev.py dev` runs the API server and Vite together (`http://localhost:5173`); Vite proxies `/api` and `/ws` to `MIZUOTO_BACKEND` (default `http://127.0.0.1:7869`). When the API server restarts, the proxy's connection errors become one short line (`vite.config.ts`, tested in `devProxy.test.ts`). Setting up is in Development setup."],[7823,"Whisper large-v3-turbo"],[16361,"Whisper large-v3-turbo"],[9347,"Whisper large-v3-turbo; Paraformer-large (Chinese)"],[809,"Whisper large-v3-turbo；Paraformer-large（中文）"],[15608,"Whisper transcribes every one of them as the text (2.5 at 50 codes: one homophone). At an RTF over 1 the audio comes slower than it plays, so on that card IndexTTS 2 would pause between chunks; 100 codes (about 1.6 s of speech) is upstream's default and the better trade."],[7070,"Whisper 对每一条的转写都与文本一致（2.5 在 50 个编码时有一个同音字）。RTF 大于 1 时音频生成得比播放慢，所以在这块显卡上 IndexTTS 2 会在分块之间停顿；100 个编码（约 1.6 秒语音）是上游的默认值，也是更好的折中。"],[3676,"Whisper 编码器在 ASR 引擎里，不与 CosyVoice 的语音分词器共享"],[14323,"Who"],[14192,"Who is where"],[13299,"Whole"],[12530,"whole anyway, after idle components left whole; no partial loading"],[9748,"Whole or not at all (`high`)"],[15590,"Whole request"],[13016,"Whole requests (VAE included) on the real weights, 6.4–6.9 s of audio, best of three warm requests, torch 2.8:"],[12523,"Whole when it fits"],[12539,"whole: unified memory gains nothing from offloading, so no partial loading and no host copies"],[10279,"Whose voice it is and how you may use it: an optional note, stored with the voice, never required"],[12122,"Why"],[16443,"Why"],[14803,"Why a child process"],[12794,"Why it is exact"],[12876,"Why it is exact"],[15157,"Why the whole stack is not bit-identical"],[1139,"Windows"],[2189,"Windows"],[8474,"Windows"],[9677,"Windows"],[10727,"Windows"],[17011,"Windows"],[16474,"With **Settings › Speech › Transcribe reference clips without a transcript** on and speech recognition installed, Mizuoto looks in its transcript cache, else transcribes the clip first in the speak job (the plan says **transcribed first**). A library voice keeps the transcript it gets."],[17007,"With `--host` set to `0.0.0.0` or another non-loopback address, other devices on the network can connect and use everything. Mizuoto only prints a warning and does not insist on a token, so set an access token (**Settings › General › Access token**, or `mizuoto config set server.access_token <token>`). See Remote access and security."],[10432,"With `--unload`: the model to unload (default: every model not in use)"],[8906,"With `ACCEL=1`, the optional attention packages that install without a compiler: xFormers at the release `mizuoto doctor` names for the image's torch (none for a CPU build), and SageAttention 1.0.6 on CUDA builds. FlashAttention is not included: it compiles for a long time unless a wheel matches the torch, and its only wheel for torch 2.8 stops xFormers 0.0.32 from importing. Choose them under Settings › Compute › Acceleration."],[9260,"With `api_prefix=\"/voice\"` the web UI is at `<address>/voice/`, the API at `/voice/api/v1/...` and the OpenAI-compatible API at `/voice/v1/...`. The web UI derives the prefix from its own script's URL; nothing else to configure."],[12885,"With `compute.attention = fast` on the CPU every call goes through the policy, all on SDPA, no fallbacks (calls per request: F5-TTS 704, OmniVoice 896, GPT-SoVITS v4 3,044, VoxCPM 1.5 3,928, CosyVoice 2 4,688, Qwen3-TTS 4,877, IndexTTS 2 6,667, Fish Speech 7,152). Seven engines still gave identical audio; IndexTTS 2 differed by at most 2 int16 steps (86.1 dB SNR, same length), its perceiver's hand-written softmax being computed by SDPA."],[15404,"With `compute.cuda_graphs` (an NVIDIA GPU holding the backbone and the tower whole: about 44 GB in bfloat16) the decoding step runs as CUDA graphs that replay the eager kernels (`drama3/steps.py`, `generate.Decoder`). A step is the tower's graphs (the output head, the frame's draws, one graph between each two of its 13 layers' attention calls), then the backbone's on that frame (one graph between each two of its 10 softmax attention layers, the Gated DeltaNet layers, the router and the experts inside them). The attention calls run eagerly between the graphs, over caches that grow by one each step, so the caches and the attention kernels are the eager code's. The step waits for the device once, for the frame's main token and whether its logits were finite."],[15823,"With `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the model wholly on its device, `compute.compile` off) a patch is one CUDA graph per number of steps and guidance value (the attention span is the whole cache there); the DiT's noise is drawn from the graphs' generator, loaded from the request's and written back at each patch. The language models' static caches are then kept with the model while graphs are kept (the memory a request needs anyway) and go when the weights move or the model unloads. The real 0.5B and 1.5 give the same audio with and without graphs, 1.6–1.9 times faster per request."],[15362,"With `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the model wholly on its device) `generate.Decoder` keeps fixed tensors per loaded model: the slow step runs as one graph per stretch between attention calls (`LayerSteps`), and the frame's draws, repetition-aware sampling and the fast transformer as one graph. The sampling settings are device tensors filled per request, so one set of graphs serves every request. The codes are identical, 2.2–2.5 times faster per frame on the decode loop."],[9857,"With `compute.vram_mode = high` (**Whole or not at all**), Mizuoto always tries to load a model whole, whatever the catalogue's estimate and the card's free memory say, as ComfyUI does. It first moves idle models off that GPU to make room, then copies the weights. The request fails only when an allocation really fails: the code is `compute_unavailable` (`detail.reason` is `out_of_memory`; exit code 9 on the command line), and every model not in use is then unloaded from every GPU (see below). With `compute.gpu_jobs` above 1, a request short of room while another request holds the GPU first waits for it to finish (up to 10 minutes), then tries."],[8972,"With `downloads.repository` set to `mizuoto-model` (the default), the mizuoto-model mirror first;"],[8978,"With `downloads.verify_checksums` (**Verify checksums**, on by default) off, only sizes are checked."],[9691,"With `server.access_token` set, the UI shows the **Access token** dialog (\"This server asks for its access token.\"); enter it once. An API request without it gets 401 `auth_required`; send it as an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header, the `mizuoto_token` cookie or a `?token=` query parameter (see HTTP API)."],[11906,"With `tts.micro_batch` on, `TtsService._batch_group()` gives a speak job a `JobSpec.group` when the variant has the `batch` capability with `max_batch > 1`, the request has one segment, no seed (a batch draws its random numbers differently) and does not stream. The group is a hash of everything but the text. Just before calling the engine, the running job calls `JobContext.adopt(max_batch - 1)`, which takes the oldest queued jobs of its group, and sends one `SynthesisTask` whose `texts` hold every text; the engine yields text *i*'s chunks with `segment = i`, the job stores one output per job and ends the adopted ones with `complete()` / `fail()`. If the batched call fails, they are `release()`d to the queue and each runs on its own."],[10034,"With a hint to run `mizuoto doctor <engine>` on the agent"],[10050,"With a self-signed agent certificate, give that certificate as `--ca-file` on the host; the host name in the certificate is then not checked. Without `--ca-file` the system's CAs are used."],[12643,"With half the context (or one frame) the seams differ visibly, which the tests check. Qwen3-TTS's codec already decodes in chunks; CosyVoice's HiFT carries a phase that tiles would break. `tiled_1d` (overlapping tiles, cross-faded, as ComfyUI tiles audio VAEs) is no longer used by an engine here; it stays for released engine packages that call it."],[12572,"With host copies (`compute.host_copies`: `auto` keeps them while free RAM stays above `compute.ram_reserve_mb`; `on`; `off`), a parameter placed on the device keeps its host tensor, so offloading it costs no transfer: the device is a cache over RAM. A partly loaded component always keeps them (its streamed units rest there). Buffers are always copied back (a module may update one in place)."],[12295,"With it, every defaulted response field would become optional in the generated types; the split it avoids only touches `SpeakRequest`"],[15987,"With Mizuoto installed and `mizuoto webui` running, this page takes you through the first use: where to start, checking torch and the engines, what a model download does, the licence-gated engines, and finally the first synthesis. Each step is given for the web UI and the command line."],[16056,"With more than one result listed, **Download all** downloads them together."],[16518,"With more than one result, **Download all** downloads them together."],[8786,"With neither `voice` nor `voice_spec`, the model speaks in its own voice (if it has one). To check a request without running it, `POST /api/v1/tts/plan` returns the segments, the parameters that apply and the warnings. A top-level field the request does not have is ignored, so that a client sending a newer version's field keeps working, and named in the warnings (\"Ignored fields the request does not have: …\"): engine options go in `engine_options`, and `options` there would be ignored. A conversion or an edit logs such fields."],[9104,"With several machines on a local network, one machine's models can be laid out as a mirror for the others. The URLs Mizuoto reques